    {
        "name": "Leptospirosis",
        "name_ja": "レプトスピラ症",
        "symptoms": {"fever", "lethargy", "vomiting", "excessive_urination", "appetite_loss", "excessive_thirst"},
        "description": "Bacterial zoonosis caused by pathogenic Leptospira spp. Affects kidneys, liver, lungs, and CNS. Transmission via contact with urine-contaminated water/soil from reservoir animals (rats, raccoons, opossums, deer). Common serovars: L. canicola, L. icterohaemorrhagiae, L. pomona, L. grippotyphosa, L. bratislava. High risk: outdoor dogs, hunting dogs, dogs near water bodies. IMPORTANT ZOONOSIS — strict barrier nursing required; human staff must wear gloves/gown/eye protection when handling urine.",
        "description_ja": "病原性Leptospira属菌による細菌性人獣共通感染症。腎臓・肝臓・肺・CNSに影響。感染源動物（ネズミ・アライグマ・オポッサム・シカ）の尿に汚染された水・土壌との接触で感染。主要血清型：L. canicola、L. icterohaemorrhagiae、L. pomona、L. grippotyphosa等。外飼い犬・猟犬・水辺活動犬がハイリスク。重要：人畜共通感染症のため、尿取扱い時は厳格なバリアナーシング（手袋・ガウン・眼保護）が必須。",
        "pathophysiology": "Leptospira penetrate intact or abraded mucous membranes or damaged skin → leptospiremia (days 4-7) with endothelial damage via outer membrane proteins (LipL32, LPS). Endothelial injury triggers: (1) platelet aggregation and consumption → thrombocytopenia; (2) coagulation cascade activation → DIC in severe cases; (3) inflammatory cytokine release (TNF-alpha, IL-1, IL-6). Renal pathology: leptospires invade proximal renal tubular cells → tubulointerstitial nephritis → oliguric or polyuric AKI (oliguric = worse prognosis). Immune-complex deposition also contributes. Hepatic pathology: direct hepatocellular necrosis + cholestasis → elevated ALT/ALP/bilirubin + coagulopathy. Pulmonary hemorrhage syndrome (LPHS): diffuse alveolar hemorrhage from pulmonary capillary vasculitis — often fatal. Uveitis: immune-mediated, can occur weeks to months after infection.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "病原菌が粘膜・傷ついた皮膚から侵入→レプトスピラ血症（4〜7日目）で外膜タンパク（LipL32・LPS）による血管内皮傷害。内皮傷害→(1)血小板凝集・消費→血小板減少；(2)凝固系活性化→重症ではDIC；(3)炎症性サイトカイン（TNF-α、IL-1、IL-6）放出。腎病変：近位尿細管細胞への侵入→尿細管間質性腎炎→乏尿性または多尿性AKI（乏尿性が予後不良）。免疫複合体沈着も関与。肝病変：直接肝細胞壊死＋胆汁うっ滞→ALT/ALP/ビリルビン上昇＋凝固障害。肺出血症候群（LPHS）：肺毛細血管炎による汎発性肺胞出血（致死率高）。ぶどう膜炎：感染後数週〜数ヶ月後に免疫介在性に発症。",
        "causes": "Leptospira interrogans (L. canicola, L. icterohaemorrhagiae, L. pomona, L. grippotyphosa etc.). Contact with urine-contaminated water/soil from reservoir animals (rats, raccoons, opossums, deer). High risk: outdoor dogs, hunting dogs, water activity dogs. Zoonosis: also infects humans.",
        "causes_ja": "Leptospira interrogans（L. canicola, L. icterohaemorrhagiae, L. pomona, L. grippotyphosa等）。感染動物（ネズミ、野生動物）の尿に汚染された水・土壌との接触。外飼い犬、狩猟犬、水辺活動犬がハイリスク。人にも感染する（人獣共通感染症）。",
        "treatment": "Two-phase antibiotic therapy: Phase 1 (leptospiremia, days 1-7): ampicillin 20 mg/kg IV q8h or penicillin G 25,000-40,000 IU/kg IV q12h — superior intravenous options for acutely ill dogs. Phase 2 (renal carrier elimination): doxycycline 5 mg/kg PO q12h x 2-3 weeks — essential to eliminate renal shedding regardless of clinical improvement. Supportive care: aggressive IV fluid therapy (LRS) for AKI — polyuric AKI requires 2-4x maintenance rates; oliguric AKI may require dopamine 2-5 μg/kg/min or furosemide 1-2 mg/kg IV; peritoneal dialysis or CRRT if oliguria refractory to medical management. Electrolyte correction: K⁺ supplementation if hypokalemic from polyuria. Monitor urine output (target >1-2 mL/kg/h); urethral catheter + closed collection system. LPHS: oxygen supplementation; avoid overhydration; transfusion if PCV <25%. Liver support: SAMe 20 mg/kg PO q24h, ursodiol 10-15 mg/kg PO q24h, Vitamin K1 if PT prolonged. Strict zoonosis precautions: patient in isolation; all staff PPE (gloves, gown, mask, eye protection); disinfect with 1:10 bleach all urine-contaminated surfaces.",
        "treatment_ja": "2段階抗菌薬療法：第1期（レプトスピラ血症）：アンピシリン20 mg/kg IV 8時間毎またはペニシリンG 25,000〜40,000 IU/kg IV 12時間毎。第2期（腎保菌排除）：ドキシサイクリン5 mg/kg PO 12時間毎×2〜3週（臨床改善後も必須）。支持療法：LRS積極的輸液（AKI管理）；多尿性AKIでは維持量の2〜4倍；乏尿性AKIではドパミン2〜5 μg/kg/分またはフロセミド1〜2 mg/kg IV；難治性乏尿では腹膜透析/CRRT。LPHS：酸素補給（過剰輸液回避）、PCV<25%で輸血。肝保護：SAMe、ウルソジオール、PT延長時ビタミンK1。人獣共通感染対策：隔離収容、全スタッフPPE着用、1:10希釈次亜塩素酸で尿汚染面消毒。",
        "prognosis": "Early treatment survival rate 80-90%. Anuric/oliguric AKI requiring dialysis has significantly worse prognosis. LPHS (pulmonary hemorrhage syndrome) often fatal. Complete renal recovery variable — some dogs have chronic kidney disease sequelae. Long-term monitoring of BUN/creatinine recommended for 6-12 months post-recovery.",
        "prognosis_ja": "早期治療で生存率80〜90%。乏尿性AKI合併例は予後が劣る（透析が必要な場合あり）。肺出血型（LPHS）は致死率が高い。腎機能の完全回復は症例による。回復後6〜12ヶ月間のBUN/クレアチニン定期モニタリングを推奨。",
        "prevention": "4-serovar Leptospira vaccine (L. canicola, L. grippotyphosa, L. icterohaemorrhagiae, L. pomona): annual booster; initial 2-dose series 3-4 weeks apart. Avoid contaminated water sources. Rodent control. Minimize wildlife contact.",
        "prevention_ja": "ワクチン接種（4価レプトスピラワクチン、年1回）。汚染水域への暴露回避。野生動物との接触制限。ネズミ駆除。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Microscopic Agglutination Test (MAT): gold standard serology; 4-fold titer rise between acute (day 0) and convalescent (day 10-14) paired samples confirms active infection; single titer >1:800 in unvaccinated dog is suggestive; identify infecting serovar (guides vaccination gaps)",
            "Leptospira PCR (whole blood in acute phase, urine in subacute): EDTA blood PCR highest sensitivity in first 7-10 days; urine PCR sensitive from day 7+ and continues during carrier phase; PCR positive = confirms current infection (unlike MAT serology)",
            "Urinalysis + urine sediment: granular casts (tubular necrosis), isosthenuria, proteinuria, hematuria, glucosuria — assess tubular damage; USG 1.008-1.012 in oliguric AKI",
            "CBC: thrombocytopenia (platelet consumption from endothelial damage), leukocytosis with left shift, anemia; platelet <50,000 = DIC risk",
            "Serum chemistry + coagulation: BUN/creatinine (AKI severity), ALT/ALP/bilirubin (hepatic involvement), PT/aPTT/D-dimer (DIC screening), albumin; repeat q24-48h during hospitalization",
            "Chest radiographs: bilateral interstitial-to-alveolar pattern suggests LPHS — critical to identify as management differs (avoid overhydration in LPHS patients)",
            "Renal ultrasound: hyperechoic kidneys with loss of corticomedullary distinction; perinephric fluid; assess kidney size (guide prognosis for CKD sequelae)",
        ],
        "urgency": "urgent",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
        "age_predisposition": "adult",
    },
    {
        "name": "Canine Infectious Hepatitis",
        "name_ja": "犬感染性肝炎",
        "symptoms": {"fever", "vomiting", "abdominal_pain", "bloated_abdomen", "lethargy"},
        "description": "Systemic viral disease caused by Canine Adenovirus Type 1 (CAV-1). Targets hepatocytes, vascular endothelial cells, and renal glomerular endothelium. Vaccination has made this rare in developed countries (CAV-2 cross-protection in combination vaccines). Routes of transmission: oronasal contact with infected urine (CAV-1 shed in urine for 6-9 months post-recovery), feces, saliva; fomite spread. Most severe in young unvaccinated dogs (<1 year). Peracute form: death within hours (DIC, cardiovascular collapse). Acute: fever, abdominal pain, hepatitis, bleeding tendency. Recovered dogs: anterior uveitis and corneal edema (hepatitis blue eye - immune complex deposition) in 20-25% of survivors. Hepatic zonal necrosis: centrilobular to massive. Intranuclear inclusion bodies (Cowdry type A) in hepatocytes and endothelial cells: pathognomonic.",
        "description_ja": "犬アデノウイルス1型（CAV-1）による全身性ウイルス疾患。肝細胞・血管内皮細胞・腎糸球体内皮細胞を標的とする。ワクチン接種が普及した先進国では稀（混合ワクチン中のCAV-2が交差防御）。感染経路：感染犬の尿（CAV-1は回復後6〜9ヶ月間尿中排泄）・糞・唾液との口鼻接触；汚染物品による伝播。最重症は若齢未接種犬（<1歳）。超急性型：DIC・循環虚脱で数時間以内に死亡。急性型：発熱・腹痛・肝炎・出血傾向。回復期：回復犬の20〜25%に前部ブドウ膜炎・角膜浮腫（肝炎ブルーアイ--免疫複合体沈着）。肝臓のゾーン性壊死：中心静脈周囲から広範性。肝細胞・内皮細胞内の核内封入体（Cowdry A型）：病理診断的所見。",
        "pathophysiology": "CAV-1 enters via oronasal route → replication in tonsils, regional lymph nodes (3-4 days) → primary viremia → dissemination to liver, spleen, kidneys, lungs, eyes. HEPATOCYTE INFECTION: CAV-1 uses CD46 (membrane complement regulatory protein) as cellular receptor → endocytosis → nuclear entry → replication → Cowdry A intranuclear inclusion body formation (early) → hepatocyte death → release of new virions. HEPATIC PATHOLOGY: Centrilobular necrosis initially (highest metabolic demand, lowest O2 tension) → extends to panlobular necrosis in severe cases. Kupffer cell activation releases inflammatory cytokines. Necrosis releases hepatocellular proteins → ALT/AST elevation. VASCULAR ENDOTHELIAL INJURY: CAV-1 directly infects endothelial cells throughout body → endothelial death → vascular permeability increase → edema, hemorrhage; petechiae/ecchymoses on serosal surfaces. DIC: endothelial activation + hepatic failure (decreased clotting factor synthesis + decreased antithrombin III) → pathological coagulation activation → consumptive coagulopathy. HEPATITIS BLUE EYE (post-recovery uveitis): immune complex (CAV-1 antigen + antibody) deposition in uveal vessels + corneal endothelium → complement activation → corneal edema (endothelial dysfunction), anterior uveitis, photophobia. Occurs 7-21 days post-recovery (as antibody titers rise). Usually self-limiting (2-4 weeks) but may cause permanent corneal scarring in severe cases. RENAL PATHOLOGY: glomerular endothelial infection → glomerulonephritis, proteinuria; tubular deposition of immune complexes.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "CAV-1が口鼻経路で侵入→扁桃/所属リンパ節で増殖（3〜4日）→一次ウイルス血症→肝・脾・腎・肺・眼への播種。肝細胞感染：CAV-1がCD46（膜補体制御タンパク）を受容体として使用→エンドサイトーシス→核内侵入→増殖→Cowdry A核内封入体形成（初期）→肝細胞死→新ウイルス粒子放出。肝臓病理：初期は中心静脈周囲壊死（代謝需要最大・酸素分圧最低）→重症例では汎小葉壊死。クッパー細胞活性化で炎症性サイトカイン放出。壊死がALT/AST上昇をもたらす。血管内皮傷害：CAV-1が全身内皮細胞に直接感染→内皮死→血管透過性亢進→浮腫・出血；漿膜面の点状/斑状出血。DIC：内皮活性化＋肝不全（凝固因子合成低下＋アンチトロンビンIII低下）→病的凝固活性化→消費性凝固障害。肝炎ブルーアイ（回復後ブドウ膜炎）：免疫複合体（CAV-1抗原＋抗体）が眼内血管/角膜内皮に沈着→補体活性化→角膜浮腫（内皮機能不全）・前部ブドウ膜炎・羞明。回復後7〜21日で発症（抗体価上昇と同期）。通常は自己限定的（2〜4週）だが重症例では永久的角膜瘢痕。腎臓病理：糸球体内皮感染→糸球体腎炎・タンパク尿。",
        "causes": "Canine Adenovirus Type 1 (CAV-1), family Adenoviridae. Highly stable in environment (survives months at room temperature). Susceptible hosts: unvaccinated dogs, foxes, wolves, coyotes, bears. Cross-protective immunity from CAV-2 vaccine (used in modern combination vaccines to avoid blue eye reaction from CAV-1 vaccine).",
        "causes_ja": "犬アデノウイルス1型（CAV-1）、アデノウイルス科。環境中に高度安定（室温で数ヶ月生存）。感受性宿主：未接種犬・キツネ・オオカミ・コヨーテ・クマ。CAV-2ワクチン（現在の混合ワクチンに使用--CAV-1ワクチンによるブルーアイ反応回避のため）からの交差防御免疫。",
        "treatment": "SUPPORTIVE (no specific antiviral available): (1) IV fluid therapy: LRS or Plasmalyte for circulatory support, correction of dehydration; glucose supplementation if hypoglycemic (hepatic failure). (2) Fresh frozen plasma (FFP) 10-15 mL/kg IV: replacement of clotting factors (DIC or severe hepatic failure); essential in hemorrhagic cases. (3) Vitamin K1 1.0 mg/kg SC q12h x3 doses: if coagulopathy present (may have vitamin K absorption impairment from hepatic disease). (4) Blood transfusion: if PCV <20% from hemorrhagic complications. (5) Hepatoprotective agents: SAMe (S-adenosylmethionine) 20 mg/kg PO q24h; silymarin (milk thistle) 50-70 mg/kg/day PO; N-acetylcysteine 140 mg/kg IV (loading dose over 15 min) then 70 mg/kg q6h IV x4-5 doses (antioxidant + glutathione precursor). (6) Antiemetics: maropitant 1 mg/kg SC q24h; ondansetron 0.1-0.2 mg/kg IV q8h. (7) H2 blocker/PPI: famotidine 0.5 mg/kg IV/PO q12h; gastrointestinal protection. (8) Broad-spectrum antibiotics (amoxicillin-clavulanate 12.5 mg/kg PO q12h; metronidazole 15 mg/kg PO q12h): prevent secondary bacterial infection (hepatic Kupffer cell dysfunction + transmucosal translocation). (9) HEPATITIS BLUE EYE (corneal edema/uveitis): topical 1% atropine q12-24h (cycloplegia - prevents synechia); topical corticosteroids (prednisolone acetate 1% q6h) if no corneal ulcers - treat uveitis; systemic NSAIDs if corneal involvement; usually resolves within 2-4 weeks. (10) STRICT ISOLATION: highly contagious; disinfect with bleach 1:32 (sodium hypochlorite).",
        "treatment_ja": "支持療法（特異的抗ウイルス薬なし）：(1)輸液療法：LRSまたはPlasmalyte（循環維持・脱水補正）；低血糖（肝不全）にはブドウ糖補充。(2)新鮮凍結血漿（FFP）10〜15 mL/kg IV：凝固因子補充（DICまたは重篤な肝不全）；出血症例では必須。(3)ビタミンK1 1.0 mg/kg SC q12h×3回：凝固障害合併時。(4)輸血：PCV<20%（出血性合併症）。(5)肝保護薬：SAMe 20 mg/kg PO q24h；シリマリン50〜70 mg/kg/日PO；N-アセチルシステイン140 mg/kg IV（負荷量：15分かけて）→70 mg/kg q6h IV×4〜5回（抗酸化薬＋グルタチオン前駆体）。(6)制吐薬：マロピタント1 mg/kg SC q24h；オンダンセトロン0.1〜0.2 mg/kg IV q8h。(7)H2遮断薬/PPI：ファモチジン0.5 mg/kg IV/PO q12h。(8)広域抗菌薬（アモキシシリン/クラブラン酸＋メトロニダゾール）：二次細菌感染予防。(9)肝炎ブルーアイ（角膜浮腫/ブドウ膜炎）：アトロピン1%点眼q12〜24h（毛様体筋麻痺--後シネキア予防）；角膜潰瘍なければ局所コルチコステロイド（プレドニゾロン酢酸塩1% q6h）；通常2〜4週で消退。(10)厳格な隔離：高度伝染性；次亜塩素酸ナトリウム1:32希釈で消毒。",
        "prognosis": "Peracute (DIC/circulatory collapse): near 100% mortality within hours. Acute severe (massive hepatic necrosis): 30-80% mortality without aggressive treatment. Mild-moderate cases: good prognosis with supportive care (90%+ survival). Hepatitis blue eye: self-limiting in 80% of dogs (2-4 weeks); permanent corneal scarring in severe cases. Long-term: recovered dogs may have chronic hepatitis or renal disease from immune complex deposition. CAV-1 urine shedding continues 6-9 months after recovery.",
        "prognosis_ja": "超急性（DIC/循環虚脱）：数時間以内にほぼ100%死亡。急性重症（広範肝壊死）：積極的治療なしで死亡率30〜80%。軽度〜中等度：支持療法で良好（生存率>90%）。肝炎ブルーアイ：80%の犬で自己限定的（2〜4週）；重症例では永久的角膜瘢痕。長期的：回復犬で免疫複合体沈着による慢性肝炎・腎疾患の可能性。回復後6〜9ヶ月間のCAV-1尿中排泄が持続。",
        "prevention": "Vaccination (CAV-2 in combination DHPP - provides cross-protection against CAV-1 without inducing blue eye reaction of CAV-1 vaccine). Core vaccine: puppy series (8, 12, 16 weeks) then booster at 1 year, then q3 years. Strict isolation of suspected cases. Disinfection (sodium hypochlorite 1:32). No treatment for CAV-1 carriers.",
        "prevention_ja": "ワクチン接種（DHPPの混合ワクチン中のCAV-2--CAV-1ワクチンのブルーアイ反応なしにCAV-1に対する交差防御）。コアワクチン：子犬シリーズ（8・12・16週）→1歳時追加→3年毎。疑い症例の厳格な隔離。消毒（次亜塩素酸ナトリウム1:32）。CAV-1キャリアへの治療法なし。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Serum chemistry (ALT, AST, ALP, total bilirubin, albumin, BUN, glucose): acute massive ALT/AST elevation (hundreds to thousands IU/L); hyperbilirubinemia (jaundice); hypoalbuminemia (synthetic failure); hypoglycemia (severe hepatic necrosis); ALP elevation (cholestasis); BUN may be low (reduced hepatic synthesis)",
            "Coagulation profile (PT, aPTT, fibrinogen, D-dimer, platelet count): prolonged PT/aPTT (clotting factor synthesis failure + consumption in DIC); thrombocytopenia; D-dimer elevation; fibrinogen may be low (DIC consumption); critical for FFP transfusion decision",
            "PCR for CAV-1 (blood, urine, conjunctival swab): definitive virological diagnosis; detect acute infection; urine PCR positive for months post-recovery; useful in unvaccinated dogs with acute hepatitis",
            "Serology (CAV-1 neutralizing antibody titer): paired titers (4-fold rise = acute infection); useful post-acute phase; vaccination history complicates interpretation; IgM-specific assay for acute infection",
            "Abdominal ultrasound: hepatomegaly (acute phase), hypoechoic liver (edema/necrosis), gallbladder wall edema, abdominal effusion (protein-rich exudate), lymphadenopathy; guide liver biopsy if needed",
            "Liver biopsy (if survives acute phase): centrilobular/panlobular necrosis + Cowdry A intranuclear inclusion bodies in hepatocytes + endothelial cells (pathognomonic); IHC for CAV-1 antigen; assess severity + fibrosis for prognosis",
        ],
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
        "age_predisposition": "juvenile",
    },
