    {
        "name": "Retinal Detachment",
        "name_ja": "網膜剥離",
        "symptoms": {"circling", "eye_redness", "squinting", "aggression_change"},
        "description": "Separation of the neurosensory retina from the retinal pigment epithelium (RPE). Three types by mechanism: (1) Rhegmatogenous: retinal tear/hole - fluid enters subretinal space (rare in dogs, more common in cats). (2) Exudative/non-rhegmatogenous: fluid accumulation from systemic or ocular disease (most common in dogs) - causes: systemic hypertension (>180 mmHg), immune-mediated chorioretinitis, infectious uveitis (distemper, Brucella, Toxoplasma, Aspergillus), lymphoma/uveal neoplasia, hyperviscosity syndrome. (3) Tractional: fibrovascular membrane traction (post-inflammatory). Breed predisposition for congenital/hereditary: Sheltie Collie Eye Anomaly (CEA), Labrador Hereditary Cataract, Miniature/Toy Poodle. BILATERAL DETACHMENT: urgent - systemic cause most likely (hypertension).",
        "description_ja": "神経網膜と網膜色素上皮（RPE）の分離。機序による3分類：(1)裂孔原性：網膜裂孔/穿孔--網膜下腔への液体流入（犬では稀、猫に多い）；(2)滲出性/非裂孔原性：全身性・眼疾患による液体貯留（犬で最多）--原因：全身性高血圧（>180 mmHg）・免疫介在性脈絡網膜炎・感染性ブドウ膜炎・リンパ腫/眼内腫瘍・過粘稠度症候群；(3)牽引性：線維血管性膜による牽引（炎症後）。先天性/遺伝性素因：シェルティーCEA・ラブラドール遺伝性白内障・ミニチュア/トイプードル。両眼性剥離：緊急--全身性原因（高血圧）が最多。",
        "pathophysiology": "The retina consists of two tissue layers apposed but not fused: (1) Outer retinal pigment epithelium (RPE) - attached to Bruch membrane/choroid; (2) Inner neurosensory retina (10 layers, photoreceptors through ganglion cells). Normal adhesion maintained by: RPE pumping fluid from subretinal space, interphotoreceptor matrix (IPMX), muller cell endfeet. Detachment disrupts photoreceptor-RPE metabolic coupling (photoreceptors depend on RPE for outer segment phagocytosis, vitamin A recycling, oxygen from choriocapillaris). EXUDATIVE: Breakdown of blood-retinal barrier (BRB) from systemic hypertension (hypertensive retinopathy cascade: arteriolar vasoconstriction → endothelial injury → increased permeability) or intraocular inflammation (chorioretinitis, uveitis) forces protein-rich fluid into subretinal space. High oncotic pressure of exudate holds fluid in place. RHEGMATOGENOUS: Posterior vitreous detachment (liquefied vitreous) passes through retinal break into subretinal space, stripping retina from RPE. TRACTIONAL: Fibrovascular proliferative membranes (proliferative vitreoretinopathy, PVR) contract and physically pull retina from RPE. CONSEQUENCES: Photoreceptor death occurs within hours to days of detachment (outer segments most susceptible - no direct vascular supply). Inner layers survive longer (vitreous oxygen supply). Reattachment within 24-48h: good visual recovery. After 7-10 days: irreversible photoreceptor loss → permanent blindness in detached area. Chronic detachment: subretinal fibrosis, rosette formation, RPE metaplasia. Acute complete detachment: vision loss within minutes. Bullous detachment (visible as greyish veil behind lens on ophthalmoscopy): severe retinal folds billowing into vitreous cavity.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "網膜は2層構造で接するが融合していない：(1)外層：網膜色素上皮（RPE）--Bruch膜/脈絡膜に付着；(2)内層：神経感覚網膜（10層、光受容体〜神経節細胞）。正常接着の維持：RPEによる網膜下腔からの液体ポンピング・光受容体間マトリックス（IPMX）・ミューラー細胞終足。剥離は光受容体-RPEの代謝結合を破壊（光受容体は外節貪食・ビタミンA再生・脈絡毛細管血管からの酸素をRPEに依存）。滲出性：全身性高血圧（高血圧性網膜症カスケード：細動脈攣縮→内皮傷害→透過性亢進）または眼内炎症（脈絡網膜炎・ブドウ膜炎）による血液網膜関門（BRB）破綻→タンパク豊富な液体が網膜下腔に流入。裂孔原性：後部硝子体剥離（液化硝子体）が網膜裂孔を通って網膜下腔に流入し網膜をRPEから剥離。牽引性：線維血管性増殖膜（増殖性硝子体網膜症PVR）の収縮による物理的牽引。結果：剥離後数時間〜数日以内に光受容体死（外節が最も感受性高い--直接の血管供給なし）。剥離後24〜48時間以内の再接着：良好な視力回復。7〜10日後：不可逆的光受容体喪失→永久失明。慢性剥離：網膜下線維症・ロゼット形成・RPE化生。",
        "causes": "Systemic hypertension (most common - chronic renal disease, hyperadrenocorticism, hyperthyroidism); immune-mediated uveitis/chorioretinitis; infectious (canine distemper, Brucella canis, Toxoplasma gondii, fungal); uveal/retinal neoplasia (lymphoma, melanoma, ciliary body adenocarcinoma); hereditary (CEA, retinal dysplasia); hyperviscosity syndrome (polycythemia, multiple myeloma); post-cataract surgery complication.",
        "causes_ja": "全身性高血圧（最多：慢性腎疾患・クッシング病・甲状腺機能亢進症）；免疫介在性ブドウ膜炎/脈絡網膜炎；感染性（犬ジステンパー・ブルセラ・トキソプラズマ・真菌）；眼内/網膜腫瘍（リンパ腫・メラノーマ・毛様体腺癌）；遺伝性（CEA・網膜異形成）；過粘稠度症候群（多血症・多発性骨髄腫）；白内障術後合併症。",
        "treatment": "EXUDATIVE (HYPERTENSIVE) - MOST URGENT: (1) Blood pressure measurement - systolic >180 mmHg confirms hypertensive etiology. (2) Immediate antihypertensive: amlodipine 0.1-0.25 mg/kg PO q24h (first-line in dogs and cats) - target systolic <160 mmHg; enalapril 0.5 mg/kg PO q12-24h may be added. (3) Treat underlying cause: renal disease (ACE inhibitor + phosphate restriction), hyperadrenocorticism (trilostane), pheochromocytoma (phenoxybenzamine). (4) BP reduction within 12-24h critical for retinal reattachment - vision may return if retina reattaches within 24-72h of detachment. (5) Topical steroids (prednisolone acetate 1% q6-8h) if concurrent anterior uveitis. EXUDATIVE (INFLAMMATORY): (6) Treat systemic infection (doxycycline for Brucella, clindamycin for Toxoplasma, itraconazole for fungal). (7) Systemic immunosuppression (prednisone 1-2 mg/kg/day) for immune-mediated chorioretinitis (AFTER ruling out infectious cause). RHEGMATOGENOUS: (8) Surgical reattachment: pneumatic retinopexy (gas bubble), scleral buckling, pars plana vitrectomy with endolaser - referral to veterinary ophthalmologist; success rate 60-80% if treated within 24-48h. TRACTIONAL: (9) Vitrectomy with membrane peeling - technically demanding. GENERAL: (10) Restrict exercise to prevent further detachment. (11) Monitor IOP - concurrent glaucoma or hypotony.",
        "treatment_ja": "滲出性（高血圧性）--最も緊急：(1)血圧測定--収縮期>180 mmHgが高血圧性病因を確認。(2)即時降圧：アムロジピン0.1〜0.25 mg/kg PO q24h（犬猫の第一選択）--目標収縮期<160 mmHg；エナラプリル追加可。(3)基礎疾患治療：腎疾患（ACE阻害薬＋リン制限）・クッシング（トリロスタン）・褐色細胞腫（フェノキシベンザミン）。(4)24時間以内の降圧が網膜再接着のために重要--剥離後24〜72時間以内の再接着で視力回復の可能性。(5)前部ブドウ膜炎合併：プレドニゾロン酢酸塩1%点眼 q6〜8h。炎症性滲出性：(6)全身感染治療（ブルセラにドキシサイクリン・トキソプラズマにクリンダマイシン・真菌にイトラコナゾール）；(7)感染除外後に免疫抑制（プレドニゾロン1〜2 mg/kg/日）。裂孔原性：(8)外科的再接着：空気/ガス注入・強膜バックル・硝子体切除＋眼内レーザー；獣医眼科医への紹介；24〜48時間以内治療で成功率60〜80%。",
        "prognosis": "Exudative from hypertension (if treated within 24-72h): 60-80% visual recovery after BP control and retinal reattachment. Chronic detachment (>7-10 days): poor visual prognosis (irreversible photoreceptor loss). Hereditary (CEA, bilateral): permanent blindness if bilateral detachment. Rhegmatogenous surgical repair: 60-80% reattachment success within 24-48h. Tractional: poor (fibrovascular proliferation often recurs). Underlying systemic disease (neoplasia, renal failure): systemic prognosis determines quality of life.",
        "prognosis_ja": "高血圧性滲出性（24〜72時間以内治療）：降圧後再接着で60〜80%の視力回復。慢性剥離（>7〜10日）：不可逆的光受容体喪失で視力予後不良。遺伝性（CEA・両眼性）：両眼性剥離で永久失明。裂孔原性外科修復：24〜48時間以内で60〜80%の再接着成功。牽引性：不良（線維血管性増殖が再発しやすい）。全身性疾患（腫瘍・腎不全）：全身予後がQOLを決定。",
        "prevention": "Blood pressure monitoring in predisposed breeds and senior dogs (chronic renal disease, hyperadrenocorticism). Genetic screening in breeding stock (CEA in Collies/Shelties, hereditary cataract in Labradors). Early treatment of systemic hypertension.",
        "prevention_ja": "素因犬種および高齢犬での血圧モニタリング（慢性腎疾患・クッシング）。繁殖犬での遺伝子スクリーニング（コリー/シェルティーのCEA・ラブラドール遺伝性白内障）。全身性高血圧の早期治療。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Blood pressure measurement (Doppler): systolic >180 mmHg = hypertensive; >160 mmHg = borderline; measure 5+ readings in quiet environment; hypertensive retinopathy is most common cause of acute bilateral blindness in older dogs with CKD/HAC",
            "Indirect ophthalmoscopy (dilated pupil): bullous retinal detachment visible as grey veil behind lens; assess extent (partial vs complete), bilaterality; ERG (electroretinogram) for retinal viability in chronic detachment before surgery",
            "Chemistry panel + urinalysis: BUN/creatinine/SDMA for CKD (most common cause of secondary hypertension); urine specific gravity; proteinuria (UPC ratio > 0.5 = renal protein loss); glucose for diabetes",
            "Ocular ultrasound (B-mode): definitive detection of retinal detachment even with hyphema/cataract obscuring fundus view; shows detached retina as hyperechoic curved membrane in vitreous; assess for subretinal fluid, masses",
            "Thorough systemic workup (CBC, chemistry, UA, chest radiographs): lymphoma (common cause - uveal infiltration); hyperviscosity (PCV, total protein, serum protein electrophoresis for myeloma); Brucella serology if relevant history",
            "Infectious serology: Brucella canis titer (rapid slide agglutination - RSAT), Toxoplasma IgG/IgM, fungal antigen (Blastomyces, Aspergillus, Cryptococcus) - especially in endemic regions or immunocompromised dogs",
        ],
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
        "age_predisposition": "adult",
    },
