    {
        "name": "Granulomatous Meningoencephalitis (GME)",
        "name_ja": "肉芽腫性髄膜脳炎（GME）",
        "symptoms": {"seizures", "stiffness", "pain_on_touch", "circling", "aggression_change"},
        "description": "Non-infectious inflammatory disease of the central nervous system characterized by perivascular granulomatous inflammation. Part of the meningoencephalitis of unknown etiology (MUE) spectrum in dogs - includes necrotizing meningoencephalitis (NME, Pug encephalitis) and necrotizing leukoencephalitis (NLE). Breed predisposition: toy and small breeds (Poodle, Maltese, Pug, Chihuahua, Yorkshire Terrier, Dachshund, Bichon Frise). Sex: females more common (2x). Age: typically 2-8 years. Three clinical forms: (1) Disseminated GME: multifocal signs (most common), acute/subacute progression; (2) Focal GME: single intracranial mass lesion, mimics neoplasia; (3) Optic GME: acute blindness, papilledema, episodic progression. Rapid progression without treatment - often fatal within weeks.",
        "description_ja": "血管周囲性肉芽腫性炎症を特徴とする非感染性CNS炎症性疾患。犬の原因不明髄膜脳炎（MUE）スペクトラムの一部--壊死性髄膜脳炎（NME：パグ脳炎）・壊死性白質脳炎（NLE）を含む。好発品種：小型犬（プードル・マルチーズ・パグ・チワワ・ヨークシャー・テリア・ダックスフント・ビションフリゼ）。性差：雌が2倍多い。年齢：通常2〜8歳。3つの臨床形態：(1)播種性GME：多巣性症状（最多）、急性/亜急性進行；(2)限局性GME：単発颅内腫瘤病変（腫瘍を模倣）；(3)視神経型GME：急性失明・乳頭浮腫・エピソード性進行。治療なしでは急速進行--数週間で致死的。",
        "pathophysiology": "GME is a sterile granulomatous inflammatory process of unknown etiology. Proposed mechanisms: (1) AUTOIMMUNE T-CELL MEDIATED: perivascular infiltrates consist predominantly of T lymphocytes (primarily CD8+ cytotoxic T cells) and macrophages (forming granulomas). Breakdown of blood-brain barrier allows T cell access to CNS. Molecular mimicry with infectious agent (viral trigger - CDV, other paramyxoviruses) has been proposed - antigen not identified. (2) PATHOLOGICAL GRANULOMA FORMATION: activated macrophages surround CNS antigen (unknown) - aggregate into Virchow-Robin space perivascular cuffs - coalesce to form granulomatous lesions in brain parenchyma. (3) COMPLEMENT AND INNATE IMMUNITY: IgG deposition in vessel walls + complement activation in some cases - may contribute to endothelial injury. (4) GENETIC SUSCEPTIBILITY: breed predisposition (toy breeds) suggests genetic component - possibly MHC class II alleles governing T cell response. TISSUE DAMAGE: direct mechanical compression by expanding granuloma, cytokine (TNF-alpha, IL-1, IL-6)-mediated neuronal injury, BBB breakdown causes edema, demyelination in white matter. FOCAL GME: single large expanding granuloma (2-3 cm) resembling brain tumor - mass effect + surrounding edema causes ICP elevation. OPTIC GME: granulomatous infiltration of optic nerves and/or chiasm. NME/NLE DISTINCTION: NME (Pug, Maltese, Chihuahua) = grey matter necrosis + granulomatous inflammation; NLE (French Bulldog, Yorkshire Terrier) = white matter necrosis; histologically distinguished from GME by necrosis predominance. All forms: perivascular lymphocytic/histiocytic cuffing present.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "GMEは原因不明の無菌性肉芽腫性炎症過程。提唱される機序：(1)自己免疫性T細胞介在性：血管周囲浸潤は主にT細胞（主にCD8+細胞傷害性T細胞）とマクロファージ（肉芽腫形成）から構成。BBBの破綻によりT細胞がCNSに侵入。感染性トリガー（ウイルス--CDV等）との分子模倣が提唱されているが抗原は未同定。(2)病的肉芽腫形成：活性化マクロファージが未知のCNS抗原を包囲→ウィルヒョウ=ロビン腔の血管周囲カフに集合→脳実質内の肉芽腫性病変に合体。(3)補体と自然免疫：一部の症例で血管壁のIgG沈着＋補体活性化。(4)遺伝的感受性：品種素因（小型犬）→MHCクラスII対立遺伝子の可能性。組織傷害：拡大する肉芽腫による直接的機械的圧迫、サイトカイン（TNF-alpha・IL-1・IL-6）介在性神経傷害、BBB破綻による浮腫、白質脱髄。限局性GME：単発大型肉芽腫（2〜3 cm）が脳腫瘍を模倣--腫瘤効果＋周囲浮腫でICP上昇。NME/NLE区別：NME（パグ・マルチーズ・チワワ）=灰白質壊死＋肉芽腫性炎症；NLE（フレンチ・ブルドッグ・ヨークシャー・テリア）=白質壊死。全形態：血管周囲リンパ球/組織球性カフィング。",
        "causes": "Unknown etiology (idiopathic autoimmune). Breed and sex predisposition suggest genetic component. Proposed triggers: viral infection (canine distemper virus molecular mimicry), aberrant immune response to unknown CNS antigen. No infectious agent isolated from CSF/brain tissue.",
        "causes_ja": "原因不明（特発性自己免疫）。品種・性差素因は遺伝的成分を示唆。提唱されたトリガー：ウイルス感染（CDV分子模倣）、未知CNS抗原に対する異常免疫反応。CSF/脳組織から感染性病原体は分離されていない。",
        "treatment": "IMMUNOSUPPRESSION (mainstay): (1) Prednisolone 2-4 mg/kg/day PO initially - rapidly controls inflammation (response within days); taper over 3-6 months based on clinical response; long-term low-dose maintenance (0.5 mg/kg EOD) often required to prevent relapse. (2) Cyclosporine 5-10 mg/kg/day PO (modified cyclosporine/Atopica): calcineurin inhibitor - blocks IL-2 and T cell activation; commonly used with prednisone (steroid-sparing); monitor trough levels (target 200-400 ng/mL); improved survival compared to prednisone alone (Flegel et al., 2011). (3) Cytarabine (Ara-C) 50 mg/m2 SC q12h x4 doses, repeat q3-4 weeks: cytosine nucleoside analog - crosses BBB, inhibits DNA synthesis of rapidly dividing immune cells; strong evidence for improved survival in combination protocols; first-line combination: prednisolone + cytarabine. (4) Procarbazine 25-50 mg/m2 PO daily: alkylating agent; crosses BBB; used in combination when cytarabine fails or as maintenance; MOPP-like protocol. (5) Mycophenolate mofetil 10 mg/kg PO q12h: alternative steroid-sparing agent; good CNS penetration. (6) Lomustine (CCNU) 60-70 mg/m2 PO q6-8 weeks: lipophilic alkylating agent with excellent BBB penetration; use when refractory to above. ACUTE SEVERE (ICP crisis): (7) Mannitol 0.5-1.0 g/kg IV over 20 min for cerebral edema/ICP elevation. (8) Dexamethasone 0.2 mg/kg IV (acute neurological deterioration). FOCAL MASS (surgical option): (9) Surgical debulking for single focal lesion causing mass effect - palliative + allows histopathologic diagnosis; followed by immunosuppression. RADIATION: (10) Whole brain radiation therapy (18-24 Gy in 3 fractions) for focal GME - some centers show 1-year survival improvement.",
        "treatment_ja": "免疫抑制（主軸）：(1)プレドニゾロン2〜4 mg/kg/日PO（初期）--炎症の急速抑制（数日以内に反応）；臨床反応に基づいて3〜6ヶ月かけてテーパー；再発予防には長期維持低用量（0.5 mg/kg EOD）が多くの場合必要。(2)シクロスポリン5〜10 mg/kg/日PO（修飾シクロスポリン/アトピカ）：カルシニューリン阻害薬--IL-2とT細胞活性化を遮断；プレドニゾロンとの併用（ステロイド節減）；トラフレベル監視（目標200〜400 ng/mL）。(3)シタラビン（Ara-C）50 mg/m2 SC q12h×4回、3〜4週毎反復：シトシンヌクレオシドアナログ--BBB通過・急速分裂免疫細胞のDNA合成阻害；組み合わせプロトコルで生存改善の強力なエビデンス；第一選択組み合わせ：プレドニゾロン＋シタラビン。(4)プロカルバジン25〜50 mg/m2 PO/日：アルキル化剤；BBB通過；シタラビン失敗時または維持療法。(5)ミコフェノール酸モフェチル10 mg/kg PO q12h。(6)ロムスチン（CCNU）60〜70 mg/m2 PO q6〜8週：脂溶性アルキル化剤--優秀なBBB通過。急性重症（ICP危機）：マニトール0.5〜1.0 g/kg IV 20分かけて；デキサメタゾン0.2 mg/kg IV。限局性（外科オプション）：単発病変の腫瘍減量術＋免疫抑制。放射線：全脳照射（18〜24 Gy/3分割）で一部の限局性GMEに1年生存改善。",
        "prognosis": "Disseminated GME with prednisone alone: median survival 30-120 days. Prednisone + cytarabine combination: median survival 2-3 years in some studies (Flegel et al.). Focal GME: better than disseminated; surgical + immunosuppression sometimes achieves long-term remission. Optic GME: poor visual prognosis (permanent vision loss common). NME (necrotizing): generally poorer than classic GME (rapid necrosis). Relapse common when steroids tapered - most dogs require lifetime immunosuppression.",
        "prognosis_ja": "播種性GME＋プレドニゾロン単独：生存期間中央値30〜120日。プレドニゾロン＋シタラビン組み合わせ：一部の研究で中央値2〜3年。限局性GME：播種性より良好；外科＋免疫抑制で長期寛解の可能性。視神経型GME：視力予後不良（永久失明が多い）。NME（壊死性）：古典的GMEより一般的に悪化。ステロイドテーパー時に再発が多い--ほとんどの犬で生涯免疫抑制が必要。",
        "prevention": "No established prevention. Genetic testing not available. Avoid immunosuppressive factors (stress, concurrent disease) in predisposed breeds.",
        "prevention_ja": "確立された予防法なし。遺伝子検査なし。好発犬種では免疫抑制因子（ストレス・併発疾患）を回避。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "MRI brain + spinal cord (FLAIR, T1 with Gd, T2, DWI): hyperintense white matter lesions on FLAIR/T2; enhancing lesions (ring-enhancing focal GME); diffuse leptomeningeal enhancement; periventricular distribution; multifocal or single mass lesion - cannot definitively distinguish from neoplasia without CSF/biopsy",
            "CSF analysis (after MRI, rule out ICP elevation): lymphocytic/monocytic pleocytosis (40-200 cells/microL); elevated protein (>25 mg/dL); glucose normal; no organisms on gram stain/culture; flow cytometry for neoplastic lymphocytes (rule out CNS lymphoma)",
            "Infectious disease panel (CSF + serum): distemper PCR (CSF); Cryptococcus antigen; Neospora caninum/Toxoplasma titer; Bartonella PCR (serum); Aspergillus if MRI shows hyphal invasion; essential to exclude infectious encephalitis before immunosuppression",
            "CBC + chemistry + urinalysis: pre-immunosuppression baseline; screen for concurrent disease; serum protein electrophoresis (hyperglobulinemia in immune-mediated disease); liver function (cyclosporine/lomustine hepatotoxicity monitoring)",
            "Brain biopsy (stereotactic): definitive histopathological diagnosis (perivascular granulomatous inflammation - macrophages + lymphocytes + plasma cells); distinguish GME from NME/NLE/neoplasia; reserved for focal mass lesions or diagnostic uncertainty after MRI + CSF",
            "Ophthalmic examination (fundoscopy): papilledema (elevated ICP), optic neuritis, anterior uveitis - optic GME form; perivascular retinal granulomata; retinal detachment (secondary to choroiditis); essential in any acute-onset blindness",
        ],
        "urgency": "high",
        "onset_pattern": "subacute",
        "age_predisposition": "adult",
    },
