    {
        "name": "Lead Poisoning",
        "name_ja": "鉛中毒",
        "symptoms": {"vomiting", "seizures", "lethargy", "appetite_loss"},
        "description": "Acute or chronic lead toxicosis causing GI, neurological, and hematological abnormalities. Most common exposure: lead-based paint chips from older buildings during renovation. Subclinical chronic exposure produces anemia and behavioral changes; acute high-dose exposure causes encephalopathy and seizures. Blood lead level >40 μg/dL = clinical toxicosis; >60 μg/dL = severe/emergency. Puppies more susceptible due to exploratory behavior and higher GI absorption (50% vs 10% in adults).",
        "description_ja": "鉛中毒による消化器・神経・血液学的異常。最多暴露源：建物改装時の鉛含有ペンキ剥片。亜臨床慢性暴露は貧血と行動変化を引き起こし；急性高用量暴露は脳症とけいれんを引き起こす。血中鉛濃度>40 μg/dL=臨床中毒；>60 μg/dL=重症/緊急。子犬はより感受性が高い（探索行動と高いGI吸収率50% vs成犬10%）。",
        "pathophysiology": "Lead absorbed via GI tract (especially in puppies, up to 50% absorption) → distributes to soft tissue then bone (bone = 90% of total body lead). Mechanism: (1) Heme synthesis inhibition: δ-aminolevulinic acid dehydratase (δ-ALAD) + ferrochelatase inhibition → accumulated δ-ALA → nucleated RBCs + basophilic stippling in peripheral blood → normocytic normochromic anemia. (2) CNS: mitochondrial damage in neurons + glutamate excitotoxicity → cerebral edema, demyelination → seizures, blindness, behavior changes, ataxia. (3) GI: smooth muscle spasm (abdominal colic, vomiting, diarrhea). (4) Renal: proximal tubular dysfunction (Fanconi-like syndrome in chronic exposure). Calcium-binding proteins (S100 family) have high lead affinity — lead substitutes for calcium in neurotransmission.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "鉛はGI管から吸収（子犬は最大50%）→軟部組織→骨に分布（骨=総体内鉛の90%）。機序：(1)ヘム合成阻害：δ-アミノレブリン酸脱水酵素（δ-ALAD）＋フェロケラターゼ阻害→δ-ALA蓄積→末梢血の有核赤血球＋好塩基性斑点赤血球→正球性正色素性貧血。(2)CNS：ニューロンのミトコンドリア障害＋グルタミン酸興奮毒性→脳浮腫・脱髄→けいれん・失明・行動変化・運動失調。(3)GI：平滑筋痙攣（腹部疝痛・嘔吐・下痢）。(4)腎臓：近位尿細管機能不全（慢性暴露でファンコーニ様症候群）。カルシウム結合タンパク質（S100ファミリー）は鉛への親和性が高い—神経伝達で鉛がカルシウムの代わりになる。",
        "causes": "Lead-based paint chips/dust from pre-1977 buildings during renovation (most common). Lead fishing weights, curtain weights, tire weights, bird shot, bullets. Lead batteries (car, motorcycle — contains high-concentration lead plates/paste). Lead solder, plumbing solder (older buildings). Lead-glazed ceramics, contaminated soil near smelters/highways. Puppies more susceptible due to chewing behavior.",
        "causes_ja": "建物改装時の鉛含有ペンキの剥片/粉塵（最多—1977年以前の建物）。釣り錘・カーテン錘・タイヤ錘・弾丸/散弾。鉛バッテリー（自動車・オートバイ—高濃度鉛板/ペースト含有）。鉛はんだ・配管はんだ（古い建物）。鉛含有陶磁器の釉薬・製錬所/幹線道路近くの汚染土壌。子犬は咀嚼行動のため感受性が高い。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Blood lead level (BLL) — MOST IMPORTANT: >10 μg/dL = exposure; >25 μg/dL = subclinical toxicosis; >40 μg/dL = clinical signs; >60 μg/dL = severe/emergency chelation indicated. EDTA tube preferred (heparinized acceptable; avoid clot tube — RBC lead redistribution)",
            "CBC with differential and blood smear: nucleated RBCs (nRBCs), basophilic stippling (punctate basophilia) — pathognomonic combination for lead toxicosis; normocytic normochromic anemia; anisocytosis",
            "Abdominal radiographs: radiopaque foreign material (paint chips, fishing weights, bullets) in GI tract — identifies source still present (requires removal); gastric/intestinal lead objects",
            "Urine δ-aminolevulinic acid (δ-ALA): elevated with δ-ALAD inhibition; indirect functional marker of lead toxicosis",
            "Serum chemistry: BUN/creatinine (renal tubular toxicity), ALT/AST (hepatic involvement in severe toxicosis), electrolytes",
            "Urinalysis: glucosuria + aminoaciduria + phosphaturia without hyperglycemia = Fanconi-like proximal tubular damage (chronic lead exposure)",
        ],
        "treatment": "GI decontamination: if radioopaque lead objects seen on radiographs, REMOVE BEFORE CHELATION (chelation mobilizes GI lead → increases absorption — do NOT chelate with lead still in GI tract). Endoscopic or surgical removal of GI lead objects; cathartics (magnesium sulfate 250 mg/kg PO × 1) to speed passage of smaller fragments. CHELATION THERAPY (BLL >40 μg/dL or clinical signs): (1) Calcium EDTA (CaNa2EDTA) — drug of choice for acute/severe lead toxicosis: 25 mg/kg diluted in 5% dextrose, IV drip over 1-2 hours, q6h × 5 days (max 75 mg/kg/day); rest 5 days between courses; (2) Succimer (DMSA, dimercaptosuccinic acid) — oral chelator, safer for maintenance/outpatient: 10 mg/kg PO q8h × 10 days, then q12h × 3 weeks (preferred for chronic/mild-moderate toxicosis). Seizure management: diazepam 0.5-1 mg/kg IV → phenobarbital 2-4 mg/kg IV; avoid barbiturates that compete with lead for protein binding. Supportive care: IV fluids for diuresis + renal protection; anti-emetics (maropitant 1 mg/kg SC); GI protection (omeprazole). Monitor BLL 2 weeks after chelation — repeat chelation if BLL rebounds >40 μg/dL (bone lead redistribution).",
        "treatment_ja": "消化管除染：X線で鉛異物が見えた場合、キレート療法前に除去が必須（キレート療法はGI内の鉛を動員し吸収増加—GI内に鉛が残存している状態でキレートしない）。内視鏡/外科的除去；下剤（硫酸マグネシウム250 mg/kg PO×1）で小フラグメントの通過促進。キレート療法（BLL >40 μg/dL または臨床症状）：(1)CaNa2EDTA（カルシウムEDTA）—急性/重症の第一選択：25 mg/kg（5%ブドウ糖希釈）IV点滴（1〜2時間かけて）6時間毎×5日（最大75 mg/kg/日）；5日間休薬後に必要に応じて次のコース；(2)コハク酸（DMSA/サクシマー）—経口キレート剤、外来管理に安全：10 mg/kg PO 8時間毎×10日、その後12時間毎×3週（慢性/軽中等度に推奨）。けいれん管理：ジアゼパム0.5〜1 mg/kg IV→フェノバルビタール2〜4 mg/kg IV。支持療法：IV輸液（利尿・腎保護）・制吐薬（マロピタント）・GI保護（オメプラゾール）。キレート療法後2週間でBLL再測定—BLLが>40 μg/dLに再上昇した場合はキレート療法を繰り返す（骨からの鉛再分布）。",
        "prognosis": "Subclinical/chronic (BLL 25-60 μg/dL, no CNS signs): good to excellent with chelation + source removal — BLL normalizes within weeks. Acute encephalopathy (BLL >60-100 μg/dL, seizures): guarded — some neurological deficits may persist despite chelation. Severe acute poisoning with status epilepticus: poor, high mortality. Key: identify and eliminate lead source, remove GI lead before chelation, full chelation course completion. Prognosis worsens with delayed treatment — neural damage from lead encephalopathy may be permanent.",
        "prognosis_ja": "亜臨床/慢性（BLL 25〜60 μg/dL、CNS症状なし）：暴露源除去＋キレート療法で良好〜優良—数週間でBLL正常化。急性脳症（BLL >60〜100 μg/dL、けいれん）：慎重—キレート療法後も一部の神経学的欠陥が残存する可能性がある。重篤な急性中毒（重積状態）：不良・高死亡率。重要：鉛暴露源の特定と除去、キレート療法前のGI内鉛除去、フルキレートコースの完遂。治療遅延で予後悪化—鉛脳症による神経障害は永続的になる可能性がある。",
        "prevention": "Restrict dog access during building renovation (lead paint dust/chips). Test old paint before renovation with lead test kits. Keep all lead-containing items (fishing weights, battery terminals, bullets, solder) in inaccessible locations. Inspect environment for lead sources if unexplained neurological/GI signs in puppies. Test soil in high-traffic/industrial areas for lead contamination.",
        "prevention_ja": "建物改装中の犬のアクセス制限（鉛ペンキ粉塵/剥片）。改装前に鉛テストキットで旧塗料を確認。鉛含有物品（釣り錘・バッテリー端子・弾丸・はんだ）を届かない場所に保管。子犬に原因不明の神経/GI症状がある場合は環境の鉛暴露源を確認。高交通量/工業地域の土壌の鉛汚染を検査。",
        "urgency": "urgent",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
    },
