    # ---- Hematologic (expanded) ----
    {
        "name": "Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC)",
        "name_ja": "播種性血管内凝固症候群（DIC）",
        "symptoms": {"lethargy", "rapid_breathing", "collapse", "vomiting", "skin_redness"},
        "description": "Life-threatening systemic activation of coagulation leading to simultaneous thrombosis (microvascular occlusion) and hemorrhage (coagulation factor/platelet consumption). Always secondary to an underlying disease. Common triggers: sepsis, SIRS, neoplasia (HSA, carcinoma), severe trauma/surgery, immune-mediated hemolysis (IMHA), envenomation, obstetric complications (dystocia, placental abruption), heat stroke, GDV, acute liver failure. Clinical paradox: thrombotic phase (microthrombi in kidneys, lungs, GI tract causing MODS) + hemorrhagic phase (bleeding from puncture sites, petechiae, hematomas, internal hemorrhage). Mortality >60% even with aggressive treatment.",
        "description_ja": "凝固の全身性活性化により血栓症（微小血管閉塞）と出血（凝固因子/血小板消費）が同時に発生する生命脅威的疾患。常に基礎疾患に続発。主なトリガー：敗血症・SIRS・腫瘍（HSA・癌腫）・重篤な外傷/手術・免疫介在性溶血（IMHA）・毒素（蛇咬傷）・産科合併症（難産・胎盤剥離）・熱中症・GDV・急性肝不全。臨床的逆説：血栓期（腎・肺・消化管の微小血栓→MODS）＋出血期（穿刺部位からの出血・点状出血・血腫・内出血）。積極的治療にもかかわらず死亡率>60%。",
        "pathophysiology": "DIC is a syndrome of systemic pathological hemostasis activation with three overlapping phases: INITIATION: Trigger (sepsis, trauma, neoplasia) releases/activates tissue factor (TF, factor III) on circulating monocytes and damaged endothelial cells → TF + factor VIIa → extrinsic coagulation cascade activation → thrombin generation. In sepsis: lipopolysaccharide (LPS) → TF upregulation on monocytes/macrophages; cytokines (IL-6, TNF-alpha) enhance TF expression and suppress natural anticoagulants. PROPAGATION: Thrombin: (1) Cleaves fibrinogen → fibrin monomer → polymerizes → fibrin clot (microvascular thrombosis in multiple organs); (2) Activates platelets → platelet aggregation → platelet consumption; (3) Activates factors V, VIII, XIII (positive feedback - amplification); (4) Activates protein C → normally inhibits Va/VIIIa (anticoagulant feedback) - overwhelmed in DIC. DEPLETION/HEMORRHAGE: Massive thrombin generation consumes: fibrinogen (falls <100 mg/dL), platelets (<50,000/microL), antithrombin III, protein C/S, factors V/VIII/XIII → paradoxical hemorrhage despite initial clotting (no clotting factors left to form hemostatic plug). FIBRINOLYSIS: Plasminogen → plasmin (via tPA) → fibrin degradation → D-dimers/FDPs; antifibrinolytic defenses (PAI-1) overwhelmed → excessive fibrinolysis in late DIC. MICROVASCULAR THROMBOSIS CONSEQUENCES: Renal glomerular/tubular microthrombi → acute kidney injury; pulmonary capillary microthrombi → ARDS; GI mucosal microthrombi → hemorrhagic enteritis, bacterial translocation; adrenal cortex → cortisol deficiency (Waterhouse-Friderichsen equivalent). MICROANGIOPATHIC HEMOLYTIC ANEMIA: RBCs sheared by fibrin strands in microvasculature → schistocytes on blood smear.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "DICは3つの重複した段階を持つ全身性病的止血活性化症候群：開始期：トリガー（敗血症・外傷・腫瘍）が循環単球と損傷内皮細胞上の組織因子（TF、第III因子）を放出/活性化→TF＋第VIIa因子→外因系凝固カスケード活性化→トロンビン産生。敗血症では：LPS→単球/マクロファージのTF上方制御；サイトカイン（IL-6・TNF-alpha）がTF発現を増強し天然の抗凝固薬を抑制。増殖期：トロンビン：(1)フィブリノゲンを切断→フィブリン単量体→重合→フィブリン凝塊（多臓器の微小血管血栓症）；(2)血小板を活性化→血小板凝集→血小板消費；(3)第V・VIII・XIII因子を活性化（正フィードバック増幅）；(4)プロテインC活性化→通常はVa/VIIIaを阻害（DICでは圧倒される）。枯渇/出血期：大量のトロンビン産生がフィブリノゲン（<100 mg/dL）・血小板（<50,000/μL）・アンチトロンビンIII・プロテインC/S・第V/VIII/XIII因子を消費→逆説的出血。線維素溶解：プラスミノゲン→プラスミン（tPA経由）→フィブリン分解→D-ダイマー/FDP。微小血管血栓の結果：腎糸球体/尿細管→AKI；肺毛細管→ARDS；消化管粘膜→出血性腸炎・細菌転座；副腎皮質→コルチゾール欠乏。微小血管病性溶血性貧血：微小血管内のフィブリン線維によるRBC破砕→血液塗抹上の断片赤血球。",
        "causes": "Sepsis/SIRS (most common - gram-negative endotoxin exposure), hemangiosarcoma (HSA - tumor vascular disruption + TF release), IMHA (RBC ghost membranes activate complement + TF), acute pancreatitis, GDV, heat stroke (>41C endothelial injury), major surgery/trauma, snakebite, obstetric emergencies, acute liver failure (decreased clotting factor synthesis + decreased protein C/antithrombin).",
        "causes_ja": "敗血症/SIRS（最多--グラム陰性内毒素曝露）・血管肉腫（HSA--腫瘍血管破壊＋TF放出）・IMHA（赤血球ゴースト膜が補体＋TFを活性化）・急性膵炎・GDV・熱中症（>41C内皮傷害）・大規模手術/外傷・蛇咬傷・産科緊急事態・急性肝不全（凝固因子合成低下＋プロテインC/アンチトロンビン低下）。",
        "treatment": "TREAT UNDERLYING CAUSE (essential - DIC will not resolve without it): (1) Aggressive treatment of sepsis (IV antibiotics), GDV surgery, anti-snake venom, etc. BLOOD PRODUCTS (replace consumed factors): (2) Fresh frozen plasma (FFP) 10-20 mL/kg IV over 2-4h: replaces all clotting factors, antithrombin III, protein C/S, fibrinogen; use when PT/aPTT >1.5x normal or active bleeding; repeat q4-6h as needed. (3) Fresh whole blood (FWB): if concurrent severe anemia (PCV <20%) + coagulopathy; provides RBCs + platelets + clotting factors. (4) Cryoprecipitate 1-2 units/10 kg IV: concentrated fibrinogen (>150 mg/bag), von Willebrand factor, factor VIII, XIII; use specifically for severe hypofibrinogenemia (<100 mg/dL) or hemophilia concurrent. (5) Platelet-rich plasma (PRP) or platelet transfusion if available: when platelets <20,000/microL with active bleeding. HEPARIN (controversial, use cautiously): (6) Unfractionated heparin (UFH) 100-300 IU/kg SC q6-8h or 200-500 IU/kg CRI: activates antithrombin → inhibits thrombin and Xa; most beneficial in thrombotic phase (before hemorrhage predominates); CONTRAINDICATED if active CNS hemorrhage or severe thrombocytopenia (<10,000); pretreat with FFP (provides antithrombin substrate for heparin to work). (7) Low molecular weight heparin (LMWH, enoxaparin) 0.8-1 mg/kg SC q6-8h: more predictable than UFH. SUPPORTIVE: (8) IV fluids: maintain perfusion without causing dilutional coagulopathy. (9) Oxygen supplementation (ARDS component). (10) Vitamin K1 1 mg/kg SC (if anticoagulant rodenticide DIC contribution). MONITORING (continuous): PT, aPTT, fibrinogen, D-dimer, platelet count q4-6h; target: fibrinogen >100 mg/dL, platelets >50,000, PT <2x normal.",
        "treatment_ja": "基礎疾患の治療（必須--基礎疾患がなければDICは解決しない）：(1)敗血症への積極的IV抗菌薬・GDV手術・抗蛇毒素等。血液製剤（消費された因子を補充）：(2)新鮮凍結血漿（FFP）10〜20 mL/kg IV（2〜4時間かけて）：全凝固因子・アンチトロンビンIII・プロテインC/S・フィブリノゲンを補充；PT/aPTT>正常の1.5倍または活動性出血時に使用；必要に応じてq4〜6h反復。(3)新鮮全血（FWB）：重篤な貧血（PCV<20%）＋凝固障害の合併時。(4)クリオプレシピテート1〜2単位/10 kg IV：フィブリノゲン濃縮物；重篤な低フィブリノゲン血症（<100 mg/dL）に特異的。ヘパリン（議論あり、慎重に使用）：(5)UFH 100〜300 IU/kg SC q6〜8hまたは CRI：アンチトロンビン活性化→トロンビン/Xa阻害；血栓期（出血優位になる前）に最も有効；活動性CNS出血または重篤な血小板減少（<10,000）では禁忌；FFP前投与（ヘパリンが機能するためのアンチトロンビン基質を提供）。支持療法：輸液（灌流維持）・酸素補給（ARDS成分）。モニタリング（継続的）：PT・aPTT・フィブリノゲン・D-ダイマー・血小板数 q4〜6h。",
        "prognosis": "Mortality 60-80% even with aggressive treatment. Prognosis primarily determined by underlying cause (sepsis from perforation vs surgically corrected GDV). Early recognition and rapid treatment of underlying cause most important prognostic factor. Chronic low-grade DIC (associated with neoplasia): may stabilize with treatment of primary disease. Fibrinogen <50 mg/dL or platelet count <10,000 = extremely poor prognosis.",
        "prognosis_ja": "積極的治療にもかかわらず死亡率60〜80%。予後は主として基礎疾患によって決まる（穿孔による敗血症 vs 外科的に修正されたGDV）。早期認識と基礎疾患の迅速な治療が最重要な予後因子。腫瘍関連の慢性低グレードDIC：原疾患の治療で安定する可能性。フィブリノゲン<50 mg/dLまたは血小板数<10,000=非常に不良な予後。",
        "prevention": "Prompt treatment of DIC-triggering conditions. Prophylactic heparin in high-risk cases (HSA post-splenectomy, IMHA). Monitor coagulation in septic patients.",
        "prevention_ja": "DICトリガー条件の迅速な治療。高リスク例での予防的ヘパリン（HSA脾摘術後・IMHA）。敗血症患者の凝固モニタリング。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Coagulation panel (PT, aPTT, fibrinogen, D-dimer, platelet count): PT >1.5x normal + aPTT >1.5x + thrombocytopenia + elevated D-dimer + low fibrinogen (<100 mg/dL) = DIC scoring; ISTH DIC score >=5 = overt DIC; repeat q4-6h for treatment monitoring",
            "Blood smear: schistocytes (fragmented RBCs - microangiopathic hemolysis diagnostic); assess platelet morphology (large/activated); neutrophil toxic changes (underlying sepsis); nRBCs from marrow stress response",
            "Thromboelastography (TEG) or ROTEM: viscoelastic point-of-care test; distinguishes hypercoagulable (early DIC - increased clot strength) from hypocoagulable (late/overt DIC - reduced clot strength); guides targeted blood product use; more informative than PT/aPTT alone",
            "CBC + chemistry: severe thrombocytopenia (platelet consumption); anemia (hemorrhagic + microangiopathic); neutrophilia or neutropenia (sepsis); BUN/creatinine (renal microthrombi-AKI); ALT/bilirubin (hepatic involvement); electrolytes",
            "Identify underlying cause: blood cultures x3 (sepsis); abdominal ultrasound (HSA, GDV, pancreatitis, neoplasia); thoracic radiographs (aspiration pneumonia, ARDS); SNAP cPL (pancreatitis); serial lactate (tissue hypoperfusion)",
            "Antithrombin III (AT III) activity: reduced in DIC (consumption); <80% AT activity = significant deficit; AT III guides heparin therapy (heparin requires AT III to function - give FFP first to restore AT III before heparin)",
        ],
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
        "age_predisposition": "adult",
    },
