    {
        "name": "Ibuprofen Toxicosis",
        "name_ja": "イブプロフェン中毒",
        "symptoms": {
            "vomiting",
            "diarrhea",
            "appetite_loss",
            "abdominal_pain",
            "bloody_stool",
            "lethargy",
            "stiffness",
            "seizures",
            "straining_urinate",
        },
        "description": "Ibuprofen (Advil, Motrin) is one of the most common human NSAID ingestions in dogs. Dogs are exquisitely sensitive — therapeutic index is very narrow. Toxic dose thresholds: GI effects \u226550 mg/kg; renal injury \u2265100 mg/kg; CNS toxicity (ataxia, seizures) \u2265175-400 mg/kg. Ibuprofen half-life 3.6-4.4h in dogs (vs. 2h in humans). Unlike naproxen, ibuprofen does NOT undergo significant enterohepatic recirculation — single-dose activated charcoal is sufficient.",
        "description_ja": "犬はイブプロフェンに高感受性。毒性量：消化管\u226550 mg/kg、腎障害\u2265100 mg/kg、CNS毒性\u2265175-400 mg/kg。半減期3.6-4.4時間。ナプロキセンと異なり腸肝再循環なし→単回活性炭で十分。",
        "pathophysiology": "Non-selective COX-1/COX-2 inhibitor. Three toxicity mechanisms: (1) GI TOXICITY (COX-1 inhibition): PGE2/PGI2 maintain gastric mucus, bicarbonate, and mucosal blood flow — prostaglandin depletion → acid penetrates unprotected mucosa → erosion, ulcers, hemorrhage, potential perforation (\u226550 mg/kg). (2) RENAL TOXICITY (COX-1/2): In reduced perfusion states, renal PGE2/PGI2 maintain afferent arteriole dilation — prostaglandin depletion → afferent vasoconstriction → ischemic AKI (\u2265100 mg/kg, lower with pre-existing renal disease). (3) CNS TOXICITY (high doses \u2265175 mg/kg): mechanism unclear — possible direct neuronal effects or cerebral edema from renal failure.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "COX-1/2非選択的阻害。①GI毒性（PGE2枯渇→粘膜保護喪失→潰瘍、\u226550 mg/kg）②腎毒性（腎血管拡張PG枯渇→求心性収縮→AKI、\u2265100 mg/kg）③CNS毒性（\u2265175 mg/kg：脳浮腫・直接毒性）。",
        "causes": "Accidental ingestion of human ibuprofen tablets, liquid gels, or suspension. A 200 mg tablet in a 5 kg dog = 40 mg/kg (near GI threshold). Owners sometimes administer human ibuprofen as pain relief — a dangerous error.",
        "causes_ja": "ヒト用イブプロフェン錠剤・カプセル・懸濁液の誤飲。5 kg犬が200 mg錠1錠=40 mg/kg（GI毒性量に近い）。飼い主が鎮痛目的で投与するケースも多い。",
        "treatment": "CALCULATE mg/kg DOSE FIRST — determines treatment intensity:\n<50 mg/kg: Decontamination + monitor (rarely serious).\n50-100 mg/kg: GI protection mandatory, monitor renal values.\n100-175 mg/kg: GI + renal protection, hospitalization.\n>175 mg/kg: ICU monitoring, CNS effects possible.\n\nDECONTAMINATION (within 2h, before clinical signs):\nEmesis: 3% H2O2 1-2 mL/kg PO or apomorphine 0.03 mg/kg IV.\nActivated charcoal 1-3 g/kg PO (single dose sufficient — no significant enterohepatic recirculation).\n\nGI PROTECTION (all \u226550 mg/kg cases):\nOmeprazole 1-2 mg/kg IV or PO q12h (PPI — most effective acid suppression).\nSucralfate 0.5-1 g PO q8h (local mucosal protection — give 30-60 min separately from other oral meds).\nMisoprostol 2-5 \u03bcg/kg PO BID-TID (PGE1 analog — replaces mucosal prostaglandin) for high-dose exposures.\nIf GI hemorrhage: metronidazole + ampicillin-sulbactam.\n\nRENAL PROTECTION (\u2265100 mg/kg or signs of renal compromise):\nIV fluids LRS 3-5 mL/kg/h \u00d7 48-72h (most important renal intervention).\nUrine output monitoring (\u22651 mL/kg/h target; urinary catheter if oliguria suspected).\nFurosemide 1-2 mg/kg IV only if oliguria despite adequate fluid loading.\n\nCNS MANAGEMENT (\u2265175 mg/kg or neurological signs):\nDiazepam 0.5-1 mg/kg IV \u2192 phenobarbital 2-4 mg/kg IV if refractory.\n\nMONITOR: BUN/creatinine q12-24h \u00d7 48-72h, fecal occult blood, PCV, urine output.",
        "treatment_ja": "摂取量(mg/kg)から治療強度を決定。脱汚染（催吐+活性炭、単回で十分）→GI保護（オメプラゾール+スクラルファート+ミソプロストール）→腎保護（積極的点滴+尿量モニタ）→CNS症状（ジアゼパム、\u2265175 mg/kgで出現）。",
        "prognosis": "Good if decontamination performed within 2h (dose <100 mg/kg). Guarded for doses >175 mg/kg or when AKI develops. Ibuprofen-induced AKI is often reversible with aggressive early fluid therapy. GI perforation requires urgent surgery.",
        "prognosis_ja": "早期脱汚染で良好（<100 mg/kg）。>175 mg/kgや腎不全発症例では慎重。早期対応でAKIは可逆的なことが多い。GI穿孔は外科的対応が必要。",
        "prevention": "Store all human NSAIDs securely. Never administer human ibuprofen to dogs — veterinary NSAIDs (meloxicam, carprofen) are specifically dosed for dogs.",
        "prevention_ja": "ヒト用NSAIDの施錠保管。犬へのヒト用イブプロフェン投与を厳禁。犬用NSAID（メロキシカム・カルプロフェン）のみを使用。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Calculate ingested dose (mg/kg) IMMEDIATELY — most critical step: total tablets \u00d7 tablet strength \u00f7 body weight (kg); determines which interventions needed (GI \u226550, renal concern \u2265100, CNS concern \u2265175 mg/kg)",
            "Blood chemistry panel (Chem-14 at presentation, then q12-24h \u00d7 48-72h): BUN, creatinine, phosphorus (AKI monitoring — creatinine rise may be delayed 24-48h); ALT, AST; electrolytes",
            "Urinalysis + urine specific gravity (at presentation and q24h): isosthenuria (USG <1.008) suggests tubular injury; hematuria indicates GI or renal bleeding; target urine output \u22651 mL/kg/h",
            "CBC with differential: PCV/TP to detect blood loss from GI ulceration; leukocytosis suggests GI inflammation or perforation",
            "Fecal occult blood (every 12-24h if symptomatic): detects occult GI bleeding before visible melena; melena indicates active upper GI hemorrhage",
            "Abdominal radiographs or ultrasound (if severe GI signs or suspected perforation): free abdominal air (pneumoperitoneum) = perforation = surgical emergency; peritoneal effusion warrants abdominocentesis",
        ],
        "urgency": "high",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
        "age_predisposition": "all",
    },
    {
        "name": "Acetaminophen Toxicosis",
        "name_ja": "アセトアミノフェン中毒",
        "symptoms": {"vomiting", "lethargy", "difficulty_breathing", "swelling", "drooling", "appetite_loss"},
        "description": "Acetaminophen (paracetamol/Tylenol) poisoning causing methemoglobinemia, hepatic necrosis, and facial/paw edema. Dogs are less sensitive than cats but still toxic at >75 mg/kg (GI/hepatic) and >200 mg/kg (methemoglobinemia). Cats: any amount potentially lethal (lack glucuronidation pathway). Hepatotoxicity onset 12-24h; methemoglobinemia within 1-4h of ingestion. Specific antidote: N-acetylcysteine (NAC) — MUST be given early.",
        "description_ja": "アセトアミノフェン（パラセタモール/タイレノール）中毒によるメトヘモグロビン血症・肝壊死・顔面/足の浮腫。犬の毒性量：>75 mg/kg（GI/肝障害）、>200 mg/kg（メトヘモグロビン血症）。猫は少量でも致命的（グルクロン酸抱合能の欠如）。肝毒性は摂取後12〜24時間；メトヘモグロビン血症は1〜4時間以内に発症。特異的解毒剤：N-アセチルシステイン（NAC）—早期投与が必須。",
        "pathophysiology": "Acetaminophen metabolism: (1) primarily glucuronidation/sulfation (non-toxic). (2) CYP2E1 → NAPQI (N-acetyl-p-benzoquinone imine) — highly reactive metabolite. When glutathione stores depleted (toxic dose) → NAPQI accumulates → (a) hepatocyte covalent binding → centrilobular hepatic necrosis; (b) hemoglobin oxidation → methemoglobin (MetHb) → impaired O2 transport → chocolate-brown mucous membranes, cyanosis; (c) Heinz body formation in RBCs → hemolytic anemia. Dogs: hepatotoxicity predominates (>75 mg/kg). Facial/paw edema: unique to dogs — unclear mechanism (possibly protein adduct-induced vascular permeability). Cats: lack glucuronidation → NAPQI overwhelms sulfation → extreme sensitivity.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "アセトアミノフェン代謝：(1)主にグルクロン酸/硫酸抱合（無毒）。(2)CYP2E1→NAPQI（N-アセチル-p-ベンゾキノンイミン）—高反応性代謝物。グルタチオン枯渇（毒性量）→NAPQI蓄積→(a)肝細胞との共有結合→小葉中心性肝壊死；(b)ヘモグロビン酸化→メトヘモグロビン（MetHb）→O2輸送障害→チョコレート色粘膜・チアノーゼ；(c)赤血球内ハインツ小体形成→溶血性貧血。犬：肝毒性が主（>75 mg/kg）。顔面/足の浮腫：犬に特徴的—機序不明（蛋白付加物誘発性血管透過性亢進の可能性）。猫：グルクロン酸抱合能欠如→NAPQI が硫酸抱合を圧倒→極度の感受性。",
        "causes": "Human OTC analgesics: acetaminophen (Tylenol 325-500 mg tablets, Tylenol PM, Nyquil, combination cold/flu medications). Prescription: hydrocodone/acetaminophen combinations. Owner self-medicating pet for pain (NEVER safe without veterinary guidance). Any dose in cats is dangerous; >75 mg/kg in dogs causes hepatotoxicity.",
        "causes_ja": "ヒト用OTC鎮痛薬：アセトアミノフェン（カロナール・タイレノール325〜500 mg錠、PM製剤、感冒薬）。処方薬：コデイン/アセトアミノフェン配合剤。飼い主の自己判断での投与（獣医師の処方なしでは絶対に安全でない）。猫は任意の量が危険；犬は>75 mg/kgで肝毒性。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "MetHb measurement (co-oximetry): SpO2 may read falsely normal despite severe MetHb — pulse oximetry is UNRELIABLE for MetHb; arterial blood gas co-oximetry measures true MetHb% (>15% = symptomatic, >50% = life-threatening)",
            "Liver enzymes (ALT, AST) at presentation and q12-24h for 72h: centrilobular necrosis peak elevation 24-72h post-ingestion; total bilirubin (conjugated vs unconjugated — hemolytic component)",
            "CBC with reticulocyte count and blood smear: Heinz bodies (new methylene blue stain), anemia, reticulocytosis — check at presentation and 48-72h",
            "Serum chemistry: BUN/creatinine (renal tubular injury), albumin/total protein (hepatic synthesis failure), coagulation panel (PT/PTT — hepatic coagulopathy)",
            "Urinalysis: hemoglobinuria (hemolysis), bilirubin (hepatic failure)",
            "Acetaminophen serum level (Rumack-Matthew nomogram): quantitative confirms ingestion — useful if presentation time uncertain, but do NOT wait for result before starting NAC",
        ],
        "treatment": "GI decontamination (within 1-2 hours, dog ambulatory): apomorphine 0.03 mg/kg IV → activated charcoal 1-3 g/kg PO. N-ACETYLCYSTEINE (NAC) — ANTIDOTE (replenishes glutathione, prevents NAPQI toxicity): loading 140 mg/kg IV (diluted in 5% dextrose, over 15-30 min), then 70 mg/kg IV q4h × 7 doses (17 doses total for 68h course in severe cases); oral NAC 140 mg/kg PO loading → 70 mg/kg PO q4h × 17 doses (if IV not available — oral effective but slower). Start NAC ASAP — do not wait for laboratory results. Methemoglobin management (MetHb >20% or symptomatic): Ascorbic acid (vitamin C) 30 mg/kg IV q6h (reduces MetHb to Hb); N-acetylcysteine also reduces MetHb. Oxygen supplementation: 100% O2 by mask/hood for methemoglobinemia. SAMe (S-adenosylmethionine) 20 mg/kg/day PO: additional glutathione support. Silymarin (milk thistle) 50-100 mg/kg/day PO: hepatoprotective. Hepatic failure management: IV dextrose (2.5-5% CRI), fresh frozen plasma (10-20 mL/kg) for coagulopathy. Blood transfusion if severe hemolytic anemia (PCV <20%). Monitor liver function, MetHb, CBC daily for 72h minimum.",
        "treatment_ja": "消化管除染（摂取後1〜2時間以内、意識明瞭）：アポモルヒネ0.03 mg/kg IV→活性炭1〜3 g/kg PO。N-アセチルシステイン（NAC）—解毒剤（グルタチオン補充、NAPQI毒性予防）：負荷140 mg/kg IV（5%ブドウ糖希釈、15〜30分かけて）、その後70 mg/kg IV 4時間毎×7回（重症では17回投与で68時間コース）；IV不可の場合は経口NAC（同用量）。NAC投与は検査結果を待たずに直ちに開始。MetHb管理（MetHb >20%または症状あり）：アスコルビン酸（ビタミンC）30 mg/kg IV 6時間毎（MetHbをHbに還元）。O2補充：メトヘモグロビン血症には100%O2。SAMe 20 mg/kg/日 PO（グルタチオン補充）。シリマリン50〜100 mg/kg/日 PO（肝保護）。肝不全管理：IVブドウ糖（2.5〜5% CRI）・FFP（10〜20 mL/kg）。重篤な溶血性貧血（PCV<20%）に輸血。72時間最低でも毎日肝機能・MetHb・CBCモニタリング。",
        "prognosis": "Treated within 2-4 hours with full NAC course: good in dogs (hepatotoxic doses). Established hepatic failure (ALT >100x normal): guarded to poor. Severe methemoglobinemia (>50% MetHb): guarded — can cause fatal anemia and organ hypoxia. Cats: guarded even with aggressive treatment due to lack of glucuronidation. Dogs that survive acute hepatotoxicity: hepatic regeneration typically occurs over 2-4 weeks. Time to NAC initiation is the most critical prognostic factor.",
        "prognosis_ja": "2〜4時間以内に治療＋フルNACコース：犬（肝毒性量）では良好。確立した肝不全（ALT >100倍正常）：慎重〜不良。重篤なMetHb血症（>50%）：慎重—致命的な貧血と臓器低酸素血症を引き起こしうる。猫：グルクロン酸抱合能欠如のため積極的治療でも慎重。急性肝毒性を生存した犬：肝再生は通常2〜4週間かけて起こる。NAC開始までの時間が最も重要な予後因子。",
        "prevention": "Store ALL human medications in pet-proof containers. NEVER give acetaminophen to pets without veterinary direction. Check all combination cold/flu/pain medications for acetaminophen content. Immediate emergency veterinary care if any ingestion suspected — do not 'watch and wait.'",
        "prevention_ja": "全ての人用薬をペット防止容器に保管。獣医師の指示なしに絶対アセトアミノフェンをペットに投与しない。全ての複合感冒薬/鎮痛薬のアセトアミノフェン含有を確認。摂取疑いの場合は直ちに緊急受診—「様子観察」は不可。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
    },
    {
        "name": "Mushroom Toxicosis",
        "name_ja": "キノコ中毒",
        "symptoms": {"vomiting", "diarrhea", "lethargy", "seizures", "drooling", "abdominal_pain", "collapse"},
        "description": "Toxic mushroom ingestion with four distinct toxidrome types by mushroom species. Most dangerous: Amanita phalloides ('death cap') and Amanita virosa containing amatoxins — cause fulminant hepatic failure with 50-90% untreated mortality. Other types: muscarine (SLUDGE), ibotenic acid/muscimol (CNS), simple GI irritants (majority of cases). Wild mushroom ingestion should always be treated as an emergency — species identification is unreliable in the field.",
        "description_ja": "有毒キノコ摂取による4種類の毒性症候群。最も危険：アマニタ属のアマトキシン含有種（タマゴテングタケ・シロタマゴテングタケ—致死率50〜90%）→電撃性肝不全。その他：ムスカリン型（SLUDGE）・イボテン酸/ムシモール型（CNS）・単純なGI刺激型（症例の大多数）。野生キノコ摂取は常に緊急事態として対処—フィールドでの種同定は信頼できない。",
        "pathophysiology": "By mushroom class: (1) Amatoxin (Amanita phalloides/virosa, Galerina): alpha-amanitin → inhibits RNA polymerase II → hepatocyte mRNA synthesis failure → centrilobular-to-diffuse hepatic necrosis → acute liver failure. Onset 6-12h; hepatic failure 24-72h; delayed GI phase 6-24h. (2) Muscarinic (Inocybe, Clitocybe): muscarine → M-AChR agonism → SLUDGE signs (salivation, lacrimation, urination, defecation, GI distress, emesis) + bradycardia, miosis, bronchospasm. Rapid onset 15-30 min; rarely fatal. (3) Ibotenic acid/muscimol (Amanita muscaria/pantherina): ibotenic acid → NMDA agonism + muscimol → GABA-A agonism → CNS excitation then depression, ataxia, seizures; onset 30-120 min. (4) GI irritants (Tricholoma, Lactarius): direct mucosal irritation → vomiting/diarrhea only; rarely serious.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "キノコの種類別：(1)アマトキシン型（タマゴテングタケ/シロタマゴテングタケ等）：α-アマニチン→RNAポリメラーゼII阻害→肝細胞mRNA合成停止→小葉中心性〜びまん性肝壊死→急性肝不全。発症6〜12時間；肝不全24〜72時間；遅発性GI期6〜24時間。(2)ムスカリン型（イノシビ属・クリトシベ属）：ムスカリン→M-AChR作動→SLUDGE徴候（流涎・流涙・排尿・排便・GI症状・嘔吐）＋徐脈・縮瞳・気管支痙攣。発症15〜30分；致死的なことは稀。(3)イボテン酸/ムシモール型（ベニテングタケ等）：イボテン酸→NMDA作動＋ムシモール→GABA-A作動→CNS興奮→抑制・運動失調・けいれん；発症30〜120分。(4)GI刺激型（多数）：粘膜直接刺激→嘔吐・下痢のみ；一般的に重篤でない。",
        "causes": "Wild mushrooms growing in gardens, parks, forests — dogs attracted to odor and opportunistic ingestion. Dangerous species in Japan: Tamago Tengu-take (Amanita phalloides equivalent), Shiro Tamago Tengu-take, Tsuki-yo-take (Omphalotus japonicus — GI irritant often misidentified), Kaen-take (Trichoderma cornu-damae — severely toxic). Rainy season (tsuyu) and autumn have highest mushroom proliferation. Never identify 'safe' wild mushroom without mycologist verification.",
        "causes_ja": "庭・公園・森林に自生する野生キノコ—犬は匂いに引き寄せられ日和見的に摂取。日本の危険な種：タマゴテングタケ属（アマトキシン）・ツキヨタケ（GI刺激型、しばしば誤同定）・カエンタケ（多毒素含有）・ドクツルタケ。梅雨期・秋にキノコの発生が最多。菌類学者による確認なしに「安全な」野生キノコを同定することは不可。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Identify mushroom type if possible: save a sample (photograph or bring fragment to clinic) for toxicology reference — mushroom identification changes management dramatically (amatoxin vs muscarinic vs GI-only)",
            "Liver enzymes (ALT, AST, GGT, ALP) at presentation and q12h for 72h: amatoxin hepatic injury peaks 24-72h; baseline normal at presentation does NOT rule out amatoxin (6-12h lag)",
            "Urinalysis: amatoxin excreted in urine — urine Meixner test (specific for amatoxins) if available; also renal tubular injury markers",
            "CBC/coagulation panel (PT, aPTT, fibrinogen): hepatic failure → coagulopathy; DIC in fulminant hepatic failure",
            "Serum chemistry comprehensive: BUN/creatinine (renal involvement with some species), albumin/total protein, glucose (hypoglycemia in hepatic failure), electrolytes",
            "Bile acids (pre and post-prandial): sensitive early marker of hepatic dysfunction — can elevate before ALT/AST in amatoxin poisoning",
        ],
        "treatment": "AMATOXIN TYPE (highest priority): GI decontamination (apomorphine → activated charcoal 1-3 g/kg q4-6h × 24-48h — amatoxins undergo enterohepatic recirculation). Antidotes/hepatoprotectives (all with evidence): (1) Silibinin (silymarin IV preparation — not available in Japan; use oral silymarin/milk thistle 50-100 mg/kg/day) — inhibits hepatic amatoxin uptake; (2) N-acetylcysteine 140 mg/kg IV loading → 70 mg/kg q6h × 7 doses (glutathione replenishment); (3) Penicillin G 100,000 IU/kg/day IV CRI (competes with amatoxin for hepatic uptake — some evidence); (4) SAMe 20 mg/kg/day PO. IV fluids (aggressive): LRS 4-6 mL/kg/h × 48-72h (forced diuresis facilitates renal amatoxin excretion). Supportive: anti-emetics (maropitant), GI protection (omeprazole 1 mg/kg IV q12h), glucose CRI (hypoglycemia prevention), FFP for coagulopathy. MUSCARINIC TYPE: atropine 0.04 mg/kg IV or IM (titrate to drying of secretions, NOT to heart rate); glycopyrrolate 0.01 mg/kg IV. Do NOT use pralidoxime (not an OP — no AChE involvement). Oxygen/bronchodilator for bronchospasm. CNS TYPE (ibotenic/muscimol): diazepam 0.5-1 mg/kg IV for seizures; supportive care. GI IRRITANT TYPE: anti-emetics, fluids, sucralfate — generally resolves 12-24h.",
        "treatment_ja": "アマトキシン型（最優先）：消化管除染（アポモルヒネ→活性炭1〜3 g/kg 4〜6時間毎×24〜48h—アマトキシンは腸肝循環を受ける）。解毒剤/肝保護（全てにエビデンスあり）：(1)シリビニン（静注製剤—日本未流通；経口シリマリン/ミルクシスル50〜100 mg/kg/日で代用）—肝臓のアマトキシン取り込みを阻害；(2)NAC 140 mg/kg IV負荷→70 mg/kg 6時間毎×7回（グルタチオン補充）；(3)ペニシリンG 100,000 IU/kg/日 IV CRI（肝臓へのアマトキシン取り込みと競合）；(4)SAMe 20 mg/kg/日 PO。積極的IV輸液（LRS 4〜6 mL/kg/h×48〜72h—強制利尿によるアマトキシン腎排泄促進）。支持療法：制吐薬・GI保護（オメプラゾール）・ブドウ糖CRI・FFP（凝固障害）。ムスカリン型：アトロピン0.04 mg/kg IV or IM（分泌物の乾燥を目標に調整—心拍数ではなく）。気管支痙攣に酸素/気管支拡張薬。CNS型（イボテン酸/ムシモール）：ジアゼパム0.5〜1 mg/kg IV（けいれん）；支持療法。GI刺激型：制吐薬・輸液・スクラルファート—通常12〜24時間で解消。",
        "prognosis": "Amatoxin (untreated): mortality 50-90%. With aggressive treatment (charcoal + NAC + silymarin + penicillin + forced diuresis): survival possible, especially if treated within first 6-12 hours (before hepatic failure). Hepatic recovery may take weeks; some develop chronic hepatic fibrosis. Muscarinic type: excellent with atropine. CNS type: good with supportive care. GI irritant type: excellent. KEY PRINCIPLE: treat all unknown wild mushroom ingestions as potentially amatoxin-containing — the cost of over-treatment is low, the cost of under-treatment of amatoxin toxicosis is fatal.",
        "prognosis_ja": "アマトキシン型（未治療）：致死率50〜90%。積極的治療（活性炭＋NAC＋シリマリン＋ペニシリン＋強制利尿）：特に肝不全前（最初の6〜12時間以内）に治療できれば生存可能。肝回復に数週間かかる場合あり；慢性肝線維症に移行する例もある。ムスカリン型：アトロピンで優良。CNS型：支持療法で良好。GI刺激型：優良。重要原則：未同定の野生キノコ摂取は全てアマトキシン含有として対処すること—過剰治療のコストは低く、アマトキシン中毒の過少治療コストは致命的。",
        "prevention": "Remove wild mushrooms from garden/yard regularly. Keep dog on leash in areas with mushroom growth. 'Leave it' command training. Bring any ingested mushroom specimen (or photograph) to the vet for identification — do NOT discard. Most important: do not rely on folk identification methods (ring, cap color, cooking odor) — deadly Amanita phalloides can closely resemble edible species.",
        "prevention_ja": "庭・裏庭の野生キノコを定期的に除去。キノコが多い地域ではリードで管理。「置いて」コマンドのトレーニング。摂取したキノコの残留物（または写真）を獣医師に持参（廃棄しない）—種同定が治療を変える。最重要：民間の識別法（指輪・笠の色・加熱時の臭い）に頼らない—致死的なタマゴテングタケは食用種と酷似する。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
    },
    {
        "name": "Snail Bait (Metaldehyde) Poisoning",
        "name_ja": "ナメクジ駆除剤（メタアルデヒド）中毒",
        "symptoms": {"seizures", "excessive_panting", "drooling", "fever", "vomiting", "collapse"},
        "description": "Metaldehyde (snail/slug bait) poisoning causing rapidly escalating tremors, hyperthermia, and seizures. One of the most acutely dangerous toxicoses — can be fatal within 4-24 hours if untreated. Pellets are grain-based and palatable to dogs; seizures can develop within 30-90 minutes of ingestion. Toxic dose: 100-300 mg/kg (clinical signs); <100 mg/kg can cause tremors in sensitive dogs. No specific antidote — aggressive muscle relaxation and temperature management are critical.",
        "description_ja": "メタアルデヒド（ナメクジ/カタツムリ駆除剤）中毒による急速に悪化する振戦・高体温・けいれん。最も急性危険な中毒のひとつ—未治療で4〜24時間以内に致死的。ペレットは穀物基材で犬の嗜好性が高い；摂取後30〜90分でけいれんが発現しうる。毒性量：100〜300 mg/kg（臨床症状）；感受性の高い犬では<100 mg/kgで振戦。特異的解毒剤なし—積極的な筋弛緩と体温管理が重要。",
        "pathophysiology": "Metaldehyde → metabolized to acetaldehyde in acidic gastric environment → CNS: disrupts GABA, serotonin, and norepinephrine systems (mechanism incompletely understood) → severe generalized muscle fasciculations + tonic-clonic seizures → rhabdomyolysis → severe hyperthermia (>41°C) → DIC, acute renal failure, hepatic injury, cardiac arrhythmias. Hyperthermia from uncontrolled muscle contractions is the primary cause of end-organ damage. Seizures and hyperthermia can become self-perpetuating (status epilepticus).",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "メタアルデヒド→酸性胃環境でアセトアルデヒドに代謝→CNS：GABA・セロトニン・ノルエピネフリン系の撹乱（機序は完全には解明されていない）→重度の全身性筋線維束攣縮＋強直間代けいれん→横紋筋融解→重度高体温（>41℃）→DIC・急性腎不全・肝障害・心臓不整脈。筋収縮による高体温が臓器障害の主因。けいれんと高体温が自己持続状態（重積状態）になりうる。",
        "causes": "Metaldehyde snail and slug pellets used in gardens/vegetable patches. Pellets are grain-based (attractive to dogs — often described as 'green kibble'). Japanese brand examples: Namedogol, Namegitol. Rain/wet season increases snail activity → increased bait application. Dogs often consume large amounts before showing signs (palatability). Also found in solid fuel (Sterno/camping fuel blocks) in some regions — though less common in Japan.",
        "causes_ja": "庭・家庭菜園で使用されるメタアルデヒドのナメクジ駆除ペレット。ペレットは穀物基材（犬にとって嗜好性が高い—「緑のドッグフード」と表現されることがある）。雨季/湿潤期はナメクジ活動増加→農薬使用増加。犬はしばしば症状が出る前に大量摂取する（嗜好性）。固形燃料（キャンプ用品）にも含まれる場合あり。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "History (most important): identify metaldehyde product, amount ingested, time since ingestion — rapid decontamination window is 30-60 min",
            "Rectal temperature: IMMEDIATELY — hyperthermia (>40°C) indicates muscle fasciculation severity and guides cooling urgency; check every 15-30 min during treatment",
            "Serum chemistry and CBC: CK (rhabdomyolysis marker — can be extremely elevated >100,000 IU/L), BUN/creatinine (AKI from myoglobulinuria), ALT/AST (hepatic injury), hematocrit",
            "Urinalysis: myoglobinuria (dark-brown urine, Heme+ on dipstick without RBCs = myoglobin) — indicates rhabdomyolysis with AKI risk",
            "Coagulation panel (PT, PTT, fibrinogen, D-dimer): DIC complication of severe rhabdomyolysis/hyperthermia",
            "ECG: cardiac arrhythmias from electrolyte disturbances (hyperkalmia from rhabdomyolysis) and hyperthermia",
        ],
        "treatment": "IMMEDIATE — time-critical. Decontamination (ONLY if within 30-60 min AND dog is ambulatory without seizures): apomorphine 0.03 mg/kg IV → activated charcoal 1-3 g/kg PO. DO NOT induce emesis if seizures/tremors present — aspiration risk. EMERGENCY SEIZURE/TREMOR CONTROL (MOST URGENT): methocarbamol 22-44 mg/kg IV slowly (muscle relaxant of choice for metaldehyde — reduces peripheral tremors without respiratory depression); repeat up to 330 mg/kg/day total; THEN diazepam 0.5-1 mg/kg IV (repeat up to 3×) → phenobarbital 2-4 mg/kg IV slow if refractory → propofol CRI for status epilepticus. TEMPERATURE MANAGEMENT (concurrent): aggressive active cooling (ice water/alcohol-soaked towels to paws, cold IV fluids, cold enema) — TARGET core temp ≤39°C; stop cooling at 39°C to prevent hypothermia overshoot. IV FLUIDS: LRS 5-10 mL/kg/h (aggressive diuresis for myoglobin clearance, prevent AKI); maintain urine output >2 mL/kg/h; sodium bicarbonate (1-2 mEq/kg IV) to alkalinize urine (prevents myoglobin precipitation in tubules). Respiratory support: intubate if respiratory failure. ICU monitoring: temperature, SpO2, ECG, urine output, CK q4-6h. Hospitalize minimum 24-48h.",
        "treatment_ja": "即時対応—時間が重要。除染（摂取後30〜60分以内かつけいれん/振戦なしの場合のみ）：アポモルヒネ0.03 mg/kg IV→活性炭1〜3 g/kg PO。けいれん/振戦がある場合は催吐禁忌—誤嚥リスク。緊急けいれん/振戦管理（最優先）：メトカルバモール22〜44 mg/kg IV緩徐投与（メタアルデヒドに対する第一選択筋弛緩薬—呼吸抑制なく末梢振戦を軽減）；1日最大330 mg/kgまで繰り返し；その後ジアゼパム0.5〜1 mg/kg IV（3回まで繰り返し）→難治性にフェノバルビタール2〜4 mg/kg IV→重積状態にプロポフォールCRI。体温管理（同時進行）：積極的な能動的冷却（氷水/アルコール湿布を足に、冷たいIV輸液、冷水浣腸）—目標深部体温≤39℃；低体温オーバーシュートを防ぐため39℃で冷却中止。IV輸液：LRS 5〜10 mL/kg/h（ミオグロビン除去のための積極的利尿、AKI予防）；尿量>2 mL/kg/h維持；炭酸水素ナトリウム（1〜2 mEq/kg IV）で尿をアルカリ化（尿細管でのミオグロビン沈殿防止）。呼吸サポート：呼吸不全には挿管。ICUモニタリング：体温・SpO2・心電図・尿量・CK 4〜6時間毎。最低24〜48時間入院。",
        "prognosis": "Mild-moderate (tremors, no seizures, treated within 1 hour): good with methocarbamol + cooling. Severe (status epilepticus, hyperthermia >41°C, rhabdomyolysis): guarded to poor — mortality increases significantly with delay. Fatal cases typically involve sustained seizures, extreme hyperthermia (>42°C), and AKI from myoglobinuria. Time to treatment and severity of hyperthermia are the two most critical prognostic factors. Dogs surviving the acute phase may develop transient hepatic injury requiring 1-2 weeks of monitoring.",
        "prognosis_ja": "軽度〜中等度（振戦、けいれんなし、1時間以内に治療）：メトカルバモール＋冷却で良好。重症（重積状態・高体温>41℃・横紋筋融解）：慎重〜不良—遅延により死亡率が著しく増加。致死例は典型的に持続的けいれん・極度の高体温（>42℃）・ミオグロビン尿による AKIを伴う。治療開始までの時間と高体温の重症度が最も重要な予後因子。急性期を生存した犬は1〜2週間のモニタリングが必要な一過性肝障害を発症する可能性がある。",
        "prevention": "Use iron phosphate-based slug bait alternatives (safe for pets and wildlife). If metaldehyde must be used: apply only in enclosed/inaccessible bait stations; restrict dog access to treated areas for ≥24 hours after application. Never leave open bags or scattered pellets accessible. Metaldehyde smells and looks like kibble to dogs.",
        "prevention_ja": "リン酸鉄系ナメクジ駆除剤の代替使用（ペット・野生動物に安全）。メタアルデヒドを使用する必要がある場合：密閉/アクセス不能なベイトステーションのみで使用；散布後≥24時間は犬の処理区域へのアクセスを制限。開封した袋や散布したペレットを放置しない。メタアルデヒドは犬にとってドッグフードと同様の匂いと外見を持つ。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
    },
    {
        "name": "Lily Toxicosis",
        "name_ja": "ユリ中毒",
        "symptoms": {"vomiting", "drooling", "hiding", "appetite_loss", "lethargy"},
        "description": "Lily toxicosis in dogs is SPECIES-DEPENDENT and differs dramatically from cats. (1) PEACE LILY / CALLA LILY (Spathiphyllum, Zantedeschia): calcium oxalate crystals cause oral/pharyngeal irritation — GI symptoms only, no systemic toxicosis. (2) TRUE LILIES (Lilium, Hemerocallis/daylily): NEPHROTOXIC IN CATS only — dogs ingesting these do NOT develop renal failure; mild GI signs only. (3) LILY OF THE VALLEY (Convallaria majalis): contains cardiotoxic cardiac glycosides (convallatoxin) — can cause life-threatening bradyarrhythmias and AV block in dogs. ALWAYS identify the specific lily species — it determines the entire management approach.",
        "description_ja": "犬のユリ中毒は種類によって管理が全く異なる。（1）スパシフィラム/カラー：シュウ酸カルシウム結晶→口腔刺激のみ（全身毒性なし）。（2）真性ユリ（Lilium/Hemerocallis）：猫特有の腎毒性—犬は腎不全にならない。（3）スズラン（Convallaria）：強心配糖体（コンバラトキシン）→致死的不整脈。ユリの種類確認が最重要。",
        "pathophysiology": "Species-specific mechanisms: (1) PEACE/CALLA LILY: Pre-formed calcium oxalate raphide crystals mechanically penetrate oral/pharyngeal mucosa → immediate pain, salivation, dysphagia. Purely local — no systemic absorption. (2) TRUE LILIES: Selective proximal tubular nephrotoxicity in CATS (mechanism unknown — possibly species-specific metabolic pathway). Dogs lack this susceptibility — only transient GI irritation. (3) LILY OF THE VALLEY: Cardenolides (convallatoxin, convalloside) inhibit Na/K-ATPase → increased intracellular calcium → initially positive inotropy, then at toxic doses: bradyarrhythmias, AV block, ventricular fibrillation — mechanism identical to digoxin toxicosis.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "スパシフィラム：結晶による口腔機械的刺激（全身毒性なし）。真性ユリ：猫特有の近位尿細管毒性（機序不明）、犬は影響なし。スズラン：コンバラトキシンがNa/K-ATPase阻害→高カルシウム→不整脈（ジゴキシン毒性と同機序）。",
        "causes": "Ingestion of lily plants or plant material. Lily of the Valley is most dangerous for dogs. Florist arrangements frequently contain Lilium (toxic to cats) — identify before exposure assumed safe.",
        "causes_ja": "ユリ植物・植物素材の摂取。スズランが犬にとって最も危険。花屋のアレンジメントに含まれるユリ属（猫に危険）に注意。",
        "treatment": "TREATMENT IS SPECIES-DEPENDENT — confirm lily type immediately:\n\nPEACE LILY / CALLA LILY (oral/GI irritation only):\nRinse mouth thoroughly with water for 10-15 min.\nOffer small amount of milk or water (dilutes crystals).\nMaropitant 1 mg/kg SQ (antiemetic).\nSucralfate 0.5 g PO q8h \u00d7 2-3 days (mucosal protection).\nRarely requires hospitalization — monitor for swallowing difficulty.\n\nTRUE LILIES (Lilium, Hemerocallis — MINIMAL CONCERN FOR DOGS):\nDogs do NOT develop nephrotoxicosis from true lilies (cat-specific toxicity).\nSupportive care for GI signs: maropitant, bland diet, hydration.\nReassure owner — dog prognosis excellent.\n\nLILY OF THE VALLEY (Convallaria — CARDIAC EMERGENCY):\nEmergency: treat as digoxin toxicosis.\nDecontamination: emesis if <2h and NO arrhythmias; activated charcoal 1-3 g/kg PO.\nContinuous ECG monitoring (AV block, ventricular arrhythmias).\nAtropine 0.02-0.04 mg/kg IV for symptomatic bradycardia/AV block.\nLidocaine 2-4 mg/kg IV bolus \u2192 25-75 \u03bcg/kg/min CRI for ventricular tachyarrhythmias.\nIV fluids: maintain perfusion.\nDigoxin Fab fragments (Digibind) if available for severe refractory bradycardia.\nICU monitoring minimum 24-48h.",
        "treatment_ja": "スパシフィラム/カラー：口腔洗浄+スクラルファート（入院不要）。真性ユリ：支持療法のみ（犬に腎毒性なし、安心させる）。スズラン（心臓緊急）：活性炭→持続ECGモニタ→アトロピン（徐脈）→リドカイン（VT）→ICU管理。",
        "prognosis": "Peace lily/Calla lily: Excellent — self-limiting oral irritation. True lilies (dogs): Excellent — no nephrotoxicity (reassure owner). Lily of the Valley: Guarded to poor — cardiac glycoside toxicosis with potential for fatal arrhythmias; early treatment significantly improves outcome.",
        "prognosis_ja": "スパシフィラム：良好（自己限定的）。真性ユリ（犬）：良好（腎毒性なし）。スズラン：予後不良〜慎重（致死的不整脈リスク）。早期治療で改善。",
        "prevention": "Identify and remove Lily of the Valley from dog-accessible areas. Keep true lily species away from cats. Identify plants before allowing access.",
        "prevention_ja": "スズランをアクセス可能な場所から除去。真性ユリは猫から隔離。植物の事前確認。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Plant species identification (MOST CRITICAL FIRST STEP): obtain photos or plant sample for identification — management differs completely between peace lily (GI only), true lily (dogs minimal concern), and lily of the valley (cardiac emergency)",
            "ECG (immediate if Lily of the Valley suspected): PR prolongation, AV block (1st/2nd/3rd degree), ventricular arrhythmias — cardiac glycoside toxicosis can be rapidly fatal without ECG-guided management",
            "Blood chemistry panel (Chem-14 at presentation and 24h): BUN, creatinine (to confirm absence of renal injury in true lily exposure), electrolytes esp. potassium (hypokalemia worsens glycoside toxicity, hyperkalemia indicates ATPase inhibition)",
            "Serum potassium (IMMEDIATE if Lily of the Valley): critical for arrhythmia management — hypokalemia worsens conduction block, hyperkalemia with bradycardia indicates severe ATPase inhibition",
            "Urinalysis + specific gravity: assess renal function (mainly to confirm absence of nephrotoxicity in true lily ingestion — expected normal in dogs)",
            "Digoxin serum level (if Lily of the Valley): cross-reacts with convallatoxin on most immunoassays — positive result confirms cardiac glycoside exposure",
        ],
        "urgency": "high",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
        "age_predisposition": "all",
    },
    {
        "name": "Sago Palm Toxicosis",
        "name_ja": "ソテツ中毒",
        "symptoms": {
            "vomiting",
            "diarrhea",
            "lethargy",
            "bloody_stool",
            "appetite_loss",
            "bloated_abdomen",
            "seizures",
        },
        "description": "Cycad (sago palm, Cycas revoluta) ingestion causing fulminant hepatic failure — one of the most deadly plant toxicoses in dogs. Seeds/nuts contain the highest toxin concentration (cycasin). Mortality rate: 50-75% even with aggressive treatment. All parts toxic but seeds especially. Common ornamental plant in Japan — significant risk when planted in accessible yards or kept indoors. Lethal dose: as few as 1-2 seeds in a medium-sized dog.",
        "description_ja": "ソテツ（Cycas revoluta）摂取による電撃性肝不全—犬において最も致死的な植物中毒のひとつ。種子/ナッツに毒素濃度が最高（サイカシン）。致死率：積極的治療でも50〜75%。全部位が毒性を持つが特に種子。日本では一般的な観葉/庭園植物—犬がアクセスできる庭や屋内に植えられている場合の重大なリスク。致死量：中型犬で1〜2個の種子。",
        "pathophysiology": "Cycasin (methylazoxymethanol glucoside) in all cycad parts → gut bacterial β-glucosidase cleaves → methylazoxymethanol (MAM) released → (1) hepatic DNA alkylation → centrilobular-to-diffuse hepatic necrosis → acute liver failure (onset 24-72h); (2) direct GI mucosal injury → vomiting/diarrhea/hemorrhage (onset 15min-4h); (3) CNS: uncharacterized neurotoxin component → seizures in late stages. Seeds contain highest cycasin concentration — one seed can deliver lethal MAM dose. Delayed onset after initial GI phase leads to false reassurance.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "全ソテツ部位のサイカシン（メチルアゾキシメタノール配糖体）→腸内細菌のβ-グルコシダーゼが切断→メチルアゾキシメタノール（MAM）放出→(1)肝臓のDNAアルキル化→小葉中心性〜びまん性肝壊死→急性肝不全（発症24〜72時間）；(2)GI粘膜への直接傷害→嘔吐/下痢/出血（発症15分〜4時間）；(3)CNS：未解明の神経毒成分→後期にけいれん。種子には最高濃度のサイカシンが含まれる—1個の種子が致死的MAM用量を供給しうる。初期GI期後の遅延発症が誤った安心感を招く。",
        "causes": "Cycas revoluta (sago palm), Zamia species, Cycas circinalis, Macrozamia species. Seeds/nuts ingested while playing (dogs chew seeds as toys). Fallen seeds/fruits in yard. Indoor ornamental cycads. All cycad species are toxic; sago palm (Cycas revoluta) is most common in Japan. Growing in parks, botanical gardens, hotel gardens, roadside landscaping. Autumn seed production increases risk seasonally.",
        "causes_ja": "ソテツ（Cycas revoluta）、ザミア属、その他のソテツ科植物の種子/ナッツを摂取。犬が種子をおもちゃとして噛む。落下した種子/果実が庭に。屋内観葉ソテツ。全ソテツ種が毒性を持つ；ソテツ（Cycas revoluta）が日本では最多。公園・植物園・ホテルの庭・道路植栽にも植えられている。秋の種子産生期にリスク増加。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Liver enzymes (ALT, AST, GGT, ALP, bilirubin) at presentation and EVERY 6-12h for 72h: cycasin hepatotoxicity peaks 24-72h; normal at presentation does NOT rule out future hepatic failure — baseline then serial monitoring is CRITICAL",
            "Coagulation panel (PT, aPTT, fibrinogen, platelets): hepatic failure → coagulopathy → severe bleeding risk; PT prolongation is an ominous prognostic sign",
            "Serum glucose: hypoglycemia from hepatic failure (glucose synthesis failure) — monitor every 4-6h",
            "Serum chemistry comprehensive: BUN/creatinine, albumin/total protein (hepatic synthesis), electrolytes (Na, K — hepatic encephalopathy-related changes)",
            "CBC: anemia, thrombocytopenia (DIC from hepatic failure); neutrophilia (systemic inflammation)",
            "Abdominal ultrasound: hepatomegaly, ascites (portal hypertension from acute hepatic failure), GI wall edema",
        ],
        "treatment": "EMERGENCY — prognosis is grave without aggressive treatment started IMMEDIATELY. GI decontamination (within 1-2 hours, dog ambulatory): apomorphine 0.03 mg/kg IV (do NOT delay for laboratory results) → activated charcoal 1-3 g/kg PO q4-6h × 48-72h (cycasin undergoes enterohepatic recirculation — REPEATED charcoal is essential). HEPATOPROTECTIVE THERAPY (start immediately regardless of enzyme levels): (1) N-acetylcysteine: 140 mg/kg IV loading → 70 mg/kg IV q6h × 7 doses (replenishes glutathione, anti-inflammatory); (2) SAMe (S-adenosylmethionine): 20-40 mg/kg/day PO (hepatocyte membrane stabilization); (3) Silymarin (milk thistle): 50-100 mg/kg/day PO (anti-fibrotic, antioxidant). IV FLUIDS: aggressive LRS 4-6 mL/kg/h + dextrose (2.5-5% to maintain BG >80 mg/dL). Hepatic failure management: fresh frozen plasma 10-20 mL/kg for coagulopathy; vitamin K1 2.5-5 mg/kg SQ; lactulose 2.5-15 mL q8h PO (ammonia trapping for hepatic encephalopathy); metronidazole 7.5 mg/kg PO TID (reduce ammonia-producing gut bacteria). GI protection: omeprazole 1 mg/kg IV q12h, sucralfate 0.5-1 g q6-8h. Seizure management: diazepam 0.5-1 mg/kg IV → levetiracetam 20 mg/kg IV (avoid phenobarbital — hepatic metabolism further stresses liver). Hospitalize minimum 3-5 days.",
        "treatment_ja": "緊急—直ちに積極的治療を開始しないと予後は絶望的。消化管除染（摂取後1〜2時間以内、意識明瞭）：アポモルヒネ0.03 mg/kg IV（検査結果を待たずに）→活性炭1〜3 g/kg PO 4〜6時間毎×48〜72h（サイカシンは腸肝循環を受ける—活性炭の反復投与が必須）。肝保護療法（酵素値に関わらず直ちに開始）：(1)NAC：140 mg/kg IV負荷→70 mg/kg IV 6時間毎×7回；(2)SAMe：20〜40 mg/kg/日 PO；(3)シリマリン（ミルクシスル）：50〜100 mg/kg/日 PO。IV輸液：積極的LRS 4〜6 mL/kg/h＋ブドウ糖（BG>80 mg/dLを維持）。肝不全管理：FFP 10〜20 mL/kg（凝固障害）；ビタミンK1 2.5〜5 mg/kg SQ；ラクツロース2.5〜15 mL 8時間毎 PO（肝性脳症の窒素トラッピング）；メトロニダゾール7.5 mg/kg PO TID（アンモニア産生腸内細菌の減少）。GI保護：オメプラゾール1 mg/kg IV、スクラルファート0.5〜1 g 6〜8時間毎。けいれん管理：ジアゼパム0.5〜1 mg/kg IV→レベチラセタム20 mg/kg IV（フェノバルビタールは肝代謝でさらに肝臓を負荷するため回避）。最低3〜5日間入院。",
        "prognosis": "Very poor overall — mortality 50-75% even with aggressive treatment. Liver failure established (ALT >100x normal, prolonged PT): poor/grave. Dogs surviving beyond 72-96 hours with improving liver values: guarded but possible recovery over 2-4 weeks. Complete recovery of hepatic function possible in survivors. Negative prognostic factors: PT prolongation, severe hypoglycemia, DIC, seizures, anuric renal failure. CRITICAL: do not wait for symptoms — start treatment immediately after confirmed cycad ingestion, even if dog appears normal. The 6-24h 'window of opportunity' for GI decontamination + hepatoprotection is the only chance to alter the outcome.",
        "prognosis_ja": "全体的に非常に不良—積極的治療でも致死率50〜75%。肝不全確立（ALT>100倍正常・PT延長）：不良/絶望的。72〜96時間後も改善する肝臓値で生存した犬：慎重だが2〜4週間で回復の可能性あり。生存犬での完全な肝機能回復が可能。不良な予後因子：PT延長・重度低血糖・DIC・けいれん・無尿性腎不全。重要：症状を待つな—確定したソテツ摂取後は犬が正常に見えても直ちに治療を開始すること。GI除染＋肝保護の「治療の窓」（6〜24時間）が転帰を変える唯一の機会。",
        "prevention": "Eliminate sago palm plants from yards, gardens accessible to dogs. If keeping cycads: complete physical barrier (fence, elevated placement) so dogs cannot access seeds. Educate owners that ALL parts of cycad are toxic — seeds are especially attractive to dogs. Emergency veterinary contact immediately for any suspected ingestion. Consider pet-safe landscaping alternatives.",
        "prevention_ja": "犬がアクセスできる庭・庭園からのソテツ植物の完全撤去。ソテツを残す場合：種子に犬がアクセスできないよう完全な物理的バリア（柵・高所配置）。ソテツの全部位が毒性を持つことをオーナーに教育—種子は犬に特に魅力的。いかなる摂取疑いでも即時に緊急受診。ペット安全な植栽の代替を検討。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
    },
    {
        "name": "Blue-Green Algae (Cyanobacteria) Toxicosis",
        "name_ja": "藍藻（シアノバクテリア）中毒",
        "symptoms": {"vomiting", "diarrhea", "seizures", "collapse", "lethargy", "drooling", "difficulty_breathing"},
        "description": "Cyanotoxin poisoning from blue-green algae blooms in stagnant water — two main toxidromes: (1) Microcystin (hepatotoxin): fulminant hepatic failure within hours to days; (2) Anatoxin-a (neurotoxin): respiratory paralysis within minutes to hours ('Very Rapid Death Factor'). No specific antidote for either toxin. Summer/early autumn peak risk during warm stagnant water blooms. Dogs frequently exposed while swimming/drinking at affected water bodies — even skin contact with bloom can cause toxicosis.",
        "description_ja": "停滞水中の藍藻（シアノバクテリア）ブルームによるシアノトキシン中毒—2種類の主要毒性症候群：(1)ミクロシスチン（肝毒素）：数時間〜数日以内に電撃性肝不全；(2)アナトキシン-a（神経毒素）：数分〜数時間以内に呼吸筋麻痺（「超急速死因子」）。どちらの毒素にも特異的解毒剤なし。夏〜初秋の温暖な停滞水でのブルームが最高リスク。犬はブルーム発生水域での水泳/飲水で暴露—皮膚接触だけでも中毒になりうる。",
        "pathophysiology": "(1) Microcystins (hepatotoxin): produced by Microcystis aeruginosa, Anabaena → hepatocyte protein phosphatase 1/2A inhibition → cytoskeletal disruption → hepatocellular necrosis → acute liver failure. Absorbed via OATP (organic anion transporting polypeptide) transporters in hepatocytes. Enterohepatic recirculation prolongs toxicity. Peak liver damage 6-24h; coagulopathy from hepatic failure. (2) Anatoxin-a (neurotoxin): acetylcholine receptor (nAChR) agonist — similar mechanism to nicotine — initial stimulation then depolarization blockade → neuromuscular junction failure → respiratory muscle paralysis → death from respiratory failure within minutes to hours. Can cause death before veterinary care is reached.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "(1)ミクロシスチン（肝毒素）：ミクロシスティス・アエルギノーサ/アナバエナが産生→肝細胞のプロテインフォスファターゼ1/2A阻害→細胞骨格の崩壊→肝細胞壊死→急性肝不全。肝細胞のOATP（有機アニオン輸送ポリペプチド）トランスポーター経由で吸収。腸肝循環により毒性が延長。肝障害のピークは6〜24時間；肝不全からの凝固障害。(2)アナトキシン-a（神経毒素）：ニコチン性AChR（nAChR）作動薬—ニコチンと類似した機序—初期刺激→脱分極ブロック→神経筋接合部不全→呼吸筋麻痺→数分〜数時間以内の呼吸不全による死亡。獣医師に到達する前に死亡しうる。",
        "causes": "Cyanobacteria bloom in eutrophic (nutrient-rich) stagnant water: ponds, lakes, reservoirs, irrigation canals, swimming pools (rare). Bloom appears as green/blue-green 'paint-like' scum on water surface, pea-soup appearance, or greenish foam on shore. Risk factors: warm temperature (>20°C), still/low-flow water, high nitrogen/phosphorus (agricultural runoff). Bloom distribution is patchy — concentrated on downwind shores. Year-round in some tropical areas; summer-autumn in Japan. Exposure routes: drinking bloom-contaminated water, swimming through bloom, licking algae off coat after swimming.",
        "causes_ja": "富栄養化（栄養塩に富む）した停滞水体でのシアノバクテリアブルーム：池・湖・ダム・灌漑水路・スイミングプール（稀）。ブルームは水面上の緑/青緑色の「ペンキ状」の膜、エンドウスープ様外観、または岸辺の緑色の泡として認識できる。リスク因子：高温（>20℃）・静水/低流速・高窒素/リン（農業排水）。ブルームは分布が斑状—風下の岸に集中。日本では夏〜秋；一部の熱帯地域では年中。暴露経路：ブルーム汚染水の飲水・ブルーム中での水泳・水泳後にコートから藻を舐める。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "History: water source, bloom description (green/bluish-green scum/foam on surface = high suspicion), time since exposure — MOST CRITICAL for triage (anatoxin death can occur within minutes to 2 hours)",
            "Liver enzymes (ALT, AST, GGT, ALP, bilirubin) at presentation and q6-12h for 48h: microcystin hepatotoxicity peaks 6-24h — baseline normal does not exclude future hepatic failure",
            "Coagulation panel (PT, PTT, fibrinogen, platelets): hepatic failure → severe coagulopathy; DIC indicator",
            "Serum glucose: hypoglycemia from hepatic failure — monitor q4-6h",
            "Water sample collection: bring sample from exposure site in clean container for municipal/environmental health testing — cyanotoxin identification helps predict toxidrome type",
            "Neurological assessment (anatoxin): muscle fasciculations, respiratory effort/rate, pupil response — serial monitoring every 15 minutes in first 2 hours",
        ],
        "treatment": "EMERGENCY — no specific antidote for either toxin. ANATOXIN TYPE (respiratory paralysis): immediate intubation + mechanical ventilation if respiratory compromise; O2 supplementation; atropine 0.04 mg/kg IV may provide partial relief (anticholinergic at muscarinic receptors, though anatoxin acts at nicotinic); neostigmine NOT effective. Aggressive supportive care. MICROCYSTIN TYPE (hepatotoxic): GI decontamination (if within 1-2 hours): apomorphine → activated charcoal 1-3 g/kg q4-6h × 48h (enterohepatic recirculation). SAME protocol as sago palm/amatoxin mushroom hepatotoxicity: NAC 140 mg/kg IV → 70 mg/kg q6h × 7 doses; SAMe 20 mg/kg/day; silymarin 50-100 mg/kg/day. Cholestyramine 0.3-0.5 g/kg q8h PO (bile acid sequestrant — traps microcystin in enterohepatic circulation). IV fluids (aggressive LRS 4-6 mL/kg/h + dextrose). Liver failure: FFP 10-20 mL/kg for coagulopathy, lactulose for hepatic encephalopathy. Wash dog immediately after removal from water (prevent continued dermal absorption). BOTH TYPES: oxygen, IV fluids, anti-emetics (maropitant), seizure management (diazepam).",
        "treatment_ja": "緊急—どちらの毒素にも特異的解毒剤なし。アナトキシン型（呼吸筋麻痺）：呼吸障害があれば即時挿管＋機械換気；O2補充；アトロピン0.04 mg/kg IV（ムスカリン受容体での部分的な抗コリン効果—アナトキシンはニコチン受容体に作用するため）；ネオスチグミンは無効。積極的支持療法。ミクロシスチン型（肝毒性）：消化管除染（1〜2時間以内）：アポモルヒネ→活性炭1〜3 g/kg 4〜6時間毎×48h（腸肝循環）。ソテツ/アマトキシンキノコと同じ肝毒性プロトコル：NAC 140 mg/kg IV→70 mg/kg 6時間毎×7回；SAMe 20 mg/kg/日；シリマリン50〜100 mg/kg/日。コレスチラミン0.3〜0.5 g/kg 8時間毎 PO（胆汁酸封鎖剤—腸肝循環でミクロシスチンを捕捉）。積極的IV輸液（LRS 4〜6 mL/kg/h＋ブドウ糖）。肝不全：FFP・ラクツロース。水から出した後は直ちに犬を洗う（皮膚吸収継続を防ぐ）。両タイプ：酸素・IV輸液・制吐薬（マロピタント）・けいれん管理（ジアゼパム）。",
        "prognosis": "Anatoxin-a (neurotoxin): grave without immediate respiratory support — deaths occur within minutes to 2 hours of heavy exposure. Dogs reaching the clinic alive with respiratory support: guarded (if respiratory function can be maintained until toxin clears). Microcystin (hepatotoxin): guarded — similar to amatoxin mushroom toxicosis; mortality depends on dose and timing of treatment. Rapid treatment before hepatic failure: possible survival with 2-4 weeks of intensive care. Established hepatic failure: poor. Key: do not allow dogs near suspicious water blooms — prevention is the only reliable protection.",
        "prognosis_ja": "アナトキシン-a（神経毒素）：即時の呼吸サポートなしでは絶望的—大量暴露後数分〜2時間以内に死亡。呼吸サポートで生きたまま来院した犬：慎重（毒素がクリアされるまで呼吸機能を維持できれば）。ミクロシスチン（肝毒素）：アマトキシンキノコ中毒に類似した慎重な予後；用量と治療タイミングによる。肝不全前の迅速な治療：2〜4週間の集中治療で生存の可能性。確立した肝不全：不良。重要：疑わしいブルームが発生した水域には犬を近づけないこと—予防のみが確実な保護。",
        "prevention": "Never allow dogs to swim in or drink from water with visible green/bluish-green scum, foam, paint-like appearance, or unusual odor. Check municipal bloom alert systems (環境省/各都道府県の水質情報). After swimming in natural water bodies: immediately rinse dog with clean water before they lick coat. Report suspected blooms to local environmental health authorities. Especially vigilant in late summer/early autumn during droughts (low water volume + warm temperatures = ideal bloom conditions).",
        "prevention_ja": "緑/青緑色の膜・泡・ペンキ様外観・異臭のある水では犬を泳がせたり飲水させたりしない。藍藻ブルームアラートシステムを確認（環境省/各都道府県の水質情報）。自然水域での水泳後：コートを舐める前に直ちに清水で洗う。疑わしいブルームを地域の環境保健当局に報告。干ばつ時（低水量＋高温=理想的なブルーム発生条件）の晩夏〜初秋は特に注意。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": "acute",
    },
