            "Urinalysis with sediment (at presentation and q12h): urine specific gravity (isosthenuria USG <1.008 = earliest tubular concentration defect); granular casts indicate tubular necrosis; glucosuria without hyperglycemia = proximal tubular dysfunction (Fanconi syndrome pattern)",
